/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1 · 子块 d：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"sub":"d","par":{"shout":{"tw":[["loud",6],["call",0],["scream",3],["cry",0],["curse",3],["noise",3],["express",2],["whisper",1],["talk",2]],"en":"At the school sports day everybody shouts. My father can shout so loud that his voice carries across the whole field. He will call my name and I run faster. When our team scores, the crowd begins to scream and cry with joy. A few boys curse the referee and make a lot of noise, so a teacher tells them to express their feelings in a better way. My quiet aunt does not shout at all; she can only whisper, yet we still talk for hours. Loud or soft, her words reach me.","zh":"学校运动会那天人人都在喊。我爸喊起来响得能穿过整个操场。他一叫我的名字，我就跑得更快。我们队得分时，全场又尖叫又欢呼。有几个男孩骂裁判、闹得很吵，老师让他们换个方式表达情绪。我那位安静的姑妈从来不喊，她只能小声说话，可我们仍能聊上几个小时。无论是喊出来的还是轻声说的，她的话我都能听见。"},"sight":{"tw":[["optic",4],["visual",4],["spectacle",3],["look",2],["position",2],["deal",0],["flood",3]],"en":"The sight from the top of the hill is famous. An optic company put a telescope there, and from that position you can see a visual trick: the sun seems to rise twice. A flood of light hits the valley below, and every look through the glass costs one coin. The whole spectacle lasts two minutes. People come from the next town to see it, and they never say a word while they wait. It is still a good deal for the money. On a clear day the view reaches thirty miles, and for the rest of the week nobody talks about anything else.","zh":"山顶上的景致很有名。一家光学公司在那里放了一台望远镜，从那个位置你能看到一个视觉上的把戏：太阳像是升起了两次。一大片光倾泻到下面的山谷，每看一次收一枚硬币。整个奇观持续两分钟。人们从邻镇赶来看，等待时一句话也不说。就这个价钱来说，仍然很划算。天气晴好时视野能及三十英里，此后一整周大家都不聊别的。"},"sign":{"tw":[["signature",4],["signify",4],["mark",0],["flag",3],["write",2],["contract",0],["alarm",3],["house",0]],"en":"There was no sign on the door of the old house. The only mark I could find was a small flag on the gate and a name that somebody had been asked to write in pencil. The contract in my bag had a signature at the bottom, but I did not know what it was meant to signify. At six the alarm went off and we had to leave the room. Nobody came to explain, and the flag stayed on the gate for another twenty years. When the house was pulled down, that flag was the only thing anybody took away.","zh":"那座老房子的门上没有任何标志。我能找到的唯一记号是大门上的一面小旗，还有一个被人用铅笔写下的名字。我包里那份合同底部有个签名，但我不知道它意味着什么。六点钟警报响了，我们只好离开那个房间。没人来解释，那面小旗又在门上挂了二十年。房子拆掉时，唯一被人带走的就是那面旗。"},"stand":{"tw":[["standard",4],["stance",4],["base",0],["bear",0],["continue",2],["fight",2],["lie",1],["hold",6]],"en":"I cannot stand his stance on this question. The standard answer is to wait, but he wants to fight at once. His base is weak: he cannot bear the cost, and if he continues like this the whole plan will not hold. Everything he says seems to lie on one thin idea, and that idea is wrong. Two of his oldest friends left the room before he finished speaking. I stayed, because somebody has to tell him the truth. He will not thank me for it, but a friend who says nothing at all is not a friend.","zh":"我受不了他在这个问题上的立场。标准答案是等等看，可他想立刻开战。他的根基很弱：他承担不起这笔费用，再这样下去整个方案都撑不住。他说的每句话似乎都建立在一条单薄的想法上，而那条想法是错的。他还没说完，两个老朋友就离开了房间。我留了下来，因为总得有人告诉他真相。"},"star":{"tw":[["interstellar",4],["stellar",4],["sun",3],["ace",0],["champion",0],["idol",3],["character",2],["lead",0]],"en":"The star of our team is a quiet boy who never talks about his interstellar dreams. In the stellar light of the evening he runs faster than anyone else, and in the morning sun he trains alone before school begins. He is the ace of the school, our champion for three years, and the idol of every small child here. But his character is what I like most: he does not lead by shouting, and he never laughs at the slower boys. He left for a bigger school last year, and the sun over the field has not felt the same since.","zh":"我们队的明星是个安静的男孩，从不谈起自己星际旅行的梦想。傍晚的星光下他跑得比谁都快，清晨的太阳里他在开学前独自训练。他是学校的王牌、连续三年的冠军，也是这里每个小孩的偶像。但我最喜欢的是他的品性：他从不靠喊叫来带队，也从不嘲笑跑得慢的孩子。去年他转去了更大的学校，自那以后操场上的阳光就不一样了。"},"tell":{"tw":[["tale",4],["teller",4],["say",0],["state",0],["express",2],["answer",3],["order",0],["know",6]],"en":"Let me tell you a short tale about a bank teller. He did not say much: he would state the amount, express nothing at all, and answer only yes or no. In order to understand the man you had to know his face. People tell me he was happy in that small room behind the thick glass. He never asked about my money and he never told me his name, but for ten years we said good morning to each other every day. When the bank closed I went to say goodbye, and the glass was already gone.","zh":"让我给你讲一个关于银行出纳员的短故事。他话不多：只报出金额，不流露任何情绪，回答也无非是或否。要理解这个人，你得熟悉他的表情。人们告诉我，他在那层厚玻璃后面的小屋里其实挺快乐。他从不打听我的钱，也从不告诉我他的名字，但十年来我们每天都互道早安。银行关门那天我去道别，那层玻璃已经不在了。"},"trust":{"tw":[["trustee",4],["fiduciary",4],["believe",2],["hope",0],["credit",3],["count",3],["expect",2],["fund",6]],"en":"You cannot trust a trustee who never writes back. I still believe in him, and I hope he will return, but I do not expect it any more. The fund is small now, and the credit of the office is gone. You can count the people who still trust him on one hand; his fiduciary duty means nothing to the rest of us. His letters are still in my drawer, unopened, and I think they will stay there for a long time. The trustee was never found, and the office has since been turned into a shop.","zh":"你没法信任一个从不回信的受托人。我仍然相信他，也希望他会回来，但我已经不抱期望了。基金现在很少，那间办公室的信誉也没了。还信任他的人一只手就数得过来；他的受托责任对其余的人来说毫无意义。他的信还放在我抽屉里，没有拆开，我想它们会在那里放很久。那位受托人再没被找到，那间办公室后来改成了一家店。"},"wave":{"tw":[["waver",4],["wavy",4],["curl",0],["roll",0],["flap",3],["wake",3],["lift",3],["move",2]],"en":"A big wave hit the side of the boat. The wavy line of the water rose, curled and rolled over the deck. The sail began to flap and the wake behind us turned white. I did not move and I did not waver; the lift of the boat felt like a hand under my feet. An hour earlier the sea had been calm as a table, and by night it will be calm again. Only the rope in my hand says that any of this happened. We came in at dusk, wet through, and nobody on the shore had noticed a thing.","zh":"一个大浪打在船舷上。起伏的水线升起来，卷曲着翻过甲板。帆开始拍打，我们身后的尾迹变成了白色。我没有动，也没有动摇；船被托起来的感觉就像脚下有一只手。一小时前海面平得像桌面，到了夜里它又会平下来。只有手里这根绳子说明刚才的一切真的发生过。我们黄昏靠岸，全身湿透，而岸上的人什么也没察觉。"},"word":{"tw":[["lexical",4],["verbal",4],["phrase",0],["book",0],["news",0],["express",2],["read",6],["order",2]],"en":"One word can change a whole page. I keep a lexical notebook: every verbal form and every short phrase goes into it. When I read the news I copy the words I do not know, in order of how often they appear. A book of ten thousand words is enough to express almost everything, my teacher says, and one wrong word can cost you a friend. I have filled four notebooks since I started, and the fifth is already half full with words I use every day. In order to read them again I mark the page with a small number.","zh":"一个词就能改变整页的意思。我有一本词汇笔记本：每个动词形式和每个短语都记进去。看新闻时我把不认识的词抄下来，按出现频率排序。我老师说，一本一万词的书足以表达几乎所有东西，而一个用错的词能让你失去一个朋友。开始记以来我已经写满四个本子。为了能再读一遍，我在页边标上一个小号码。"},"water":{"tw":[["aquatic",4],["hydraulic",4],["irrigate",0],["wet",2],["dry",6],["fill",2],["sand",6]],"en":"The water in this valley comes from a spring. In summer we irrigate the fields with it, and the hydraulic pump is old but still works. The aquatic plants near the edge stay wet all year, while the sand on the far side is dry. Every evening I fill two bottles and carry them home. In winter the spring slows down and we have to walk much further for the same two bottles. My mother says the spring has never once failed us, and I hope that is still true.","zh":"这个山谷里的水来自一眼泉。夏天我们用它灌溉田地，那台水泵很旧但还能用。靠边的水生植物终年是湿的，而远处那片沙子却是干的。每天傍晚我灌满两瓶水带回家。到了冬天泉水流得慢，为同样两瓶水我们得走远得多的路。"},"sound":{"tw":[["soundly",4],["voice",0],["acoustic",6],["noise",3],["silence",1],["heavy",0],["blow",3],["announce",2],["good",5]],"en":"The sound in the old hall is beautiful. A single voice fills it, and the acoustic roof holds every note. There is no noise from the street, only a heavy silence between the songs. When the singer stops you can hear the wind blow across the roof. The man at the door will announce the next piece in a low voice. At night the whole building sleeps soundly. It is a good place to sit and think, and nobody asks you to leave. The heavy door closes behind you, and the noise of the town is simply gone.","zh":"那座旧厅里的声音很美。一个人的嗓音就能填满它，声学屋顶留住了每一个音。街上没有噪音，歌声之间只有沉沉的寂静。歌手停下时，你能听见风掠过屋顶。门口那个人会用低沉的嗓音报出下一曲。夜里整栋楼睡得很沉。那是个适合坐着想事的好地方，也没人赶你走。沉重的门在身后关上，镇上的噪音就那样消失了。"},"sing":{"tw":[["song",4],["talk",2],["chant",3],["sound",2],["tune",6],["whistle",0],["hum",3],["listen",6],["interpret",2]],"en":"Please sing that song again. My grandmother could talk about music for hours; she said every tune has a sound of its own. In the old church they chant without a book, and the children hum along. When I was small I could only whistle, never sing. I listen to the same three songs every winter, and each time I interpret the words a little differently. The last line is always the same, and that is why I remember it. If you want, we can sing it together on Sunday evening.","zh":"请把那首歌再唱一遍。我祖母谈起音乐能说上几个小时；她说每支曲子都有自己独特的声音。在那座旧教堂里，人们不看谱子吟唱，孩子们跟着哼。我小时候只会吹口哨，从不会唱。每年冬天我都听同样的三首歌，而每一次我对歌词的理解都略有不同。"},"skin":{"tw":[["skinny",4],["bark",0],["scalp",3],["hide",0],["jacket",3],["bag",2],["breast",6],["struggle",0],["climb",2]],"en":"The skin on his hands is hard and dark. He is skinny now, and his jacket hangs loose on him. A leather bag, made from the hide of an old cow, sits on the floor next to his boots. The bark of the tree outside is rough, like his scalp. He has a mark on his breast, near the throat, from a struggle twenty years ago. Every winter he has to climb the same hill twice a day. He says the cold has taken the feeling out of it, and he does not miss it.","zh":"他手上的皮肤又硬又黑。他如今很瘦，夹克挂在身上空荡荡的。一个用老牛皮做的皮包放在地上，挨着他的靴子。外面那棵树的树皮很粗糙，就像他的头皮。他胸口靠近喉咙处有一道疤，是二十年前一场扭打留下的。每年冬天他都得每天爬两次那座山。"},"speak":{"tw":[["speech",4],["address",0],["sound",2],["listen",6],["mouth",0],["shout",3],["communicate",2],["continue",3]],"en":"I cannot speak in front of a crowd. My speech was ready, but when I stood up my mouth went dry and the sound of the room was louder than my voice. People began to shout from the back. I tried to continue and then to address one man only. It is easier to listen than to speak, and much easier to keep quiet. Next time I will try to communicate something shorter. My hands shake when the room is quiet, and they shake even more when it is not.","zh":"我无法在人前讲话。讲稿早就写好了，可我一站起来嘴就发干，屋里的声音比我的嗓音还大。后面的人开始喊。我试着继续说下去，接着只对着一个人讲。听比说容易，闭嘴不说更容易。下次我要试着讲短一点。"},"state":{"tw":[["civil",4],["country",0],["propose",2],["express",2],["answer",3],["attribute",2],["law",6],["land",0],["add",3]],"en":"The state of the roads is the main question here. Our country has a new law about land, and the administration wants to add three more. I cannot propose anything better: no state can express what the farmers feel when the water comes. You can attribute the damage to the rain, but that is not the answer. The civil servants came, wrote one page and left. Every spring we wait for them to come back. The old man who keeps the records says the state of things was worse in his father's day.","zh":"道路的状况是这里的主要问题。我们国家有了一项关于土地的新法律，行政部门还想再加上三条。我提不出更好的办法：没有什么状态能表达农民在水来时的感受。你可以把损失归因于雨水，可那不是答案。公务员来了，写了一页纸就走了。每年春天我们都等着他们再回来。"},"study":{"tw":[["student",4],["consider",0],["check",3],["research",6],["field",0],["major",3],["think",2],["learn",2]],"en":"I study in the room above the shop. There is one small window and a table full of books. My sister is a student of science; she comes here to research the plants in the field behind the house. We check each other's work every evening. I think this is the only way to learn: consider one thing at a time and then leave it alone. Her major is much harder than mine. My father studied in the same room and never got further than the second book. He says a good table is worth more than a good teacher.","zh":"我在店铺楼上那间屋里学习。屋里只有一扇小窗和一张堆满书的桌子。我妹妹是学理科的学生；她到这里来研究屋后地里的植物。每天晚上我们互相检查作业。我想这是唯一的学习方法：一次只琢磨一件事，然后就放手。她的专业比我的难得多。"},"tie":{"tw":[["draw",0],["ground",3],["finish",2],["marry",0],["join",3],["relate",2],["round",6],["attach",3],["straight",6]],"en":"He wore a black tie to the wedding. The two families will join their names, and after the ceremony they will marry in the old church, on the ground floor of which his mother was born. I had to finish the flowers before nine and attach a card to each one. It is hard to relate one thing to another here. We sat round the table and nobody could draw a straight line. The knot took me ten minutes, and in the photograph it is still crooked. My mother laughed at me and tied it again in one movement.","zh":"他打了条黑领带去参加婚礼。两家人要合成一个姓，仪式之后他们将在那座老教堂里成婚——他母亲就出生在那教堂的底层。我得在九点前把花弄完，并在每一束上别一张卡片。在这里很难把一件事和另一件事联系起来。我们围着桌子坐着，没人能画出一条直线。"},"time":{"tw":[["clock",0],["dead",3],["experience",2],["clip",0],["hour",3],["term",2],["next",6],["sentence",0]],"en":"We have no time, and the clock on the wall is dead. It stopped at five past four one afternoon in June, and nobody has touched it since. Experience tells me the next hour will decide everything. The term ends on Friday, and my last sentence has to be in by then. I will clip the papers together and hand them over at the door. It is the same every year. I have written the date on every page so that I will know the time of it later. Someday someone will read these pages and count the days between them.","zh":"我们没有时间，而墙上的钟是停的。它在六月的一个下午四点零五分停了，此后没人碰过它。经验告诉我，接下来的一个小时会决定一切。学期周五结束，到那时我最后一句必须交上去。我会把纸夹在一起，在门口交出去。每年都是这样。"},"touch":{"tw":[["tactile",4],["concern",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["easy",6],["meet",0],["cover",3],["change",2],["reach",0]],"en":"Do not touch the glass. The tactile map behind it is for blind visitors, and every finger leaves a mark. I have one small concern: the cover of the case is loose. It is easy to change the paper, but you must act before the glue dries. We will meet on Thursday and catch up on the rest. The hand of the woman in the picture is reaching for the same door. The guard watches everybody's hands, and nobody has ever touched the glass twice. He stands there all day and says nothing at all.","zh":"别碰玻璃。后面那张触摸地图是给盲人访客用的，每根手指都会留下印子。我有一个小顾虑：盒子的盖子松了。换纸很容易，但必须在胶干之前动手。我们周四见面，把剩下的部分跟上。画里那个女人的手也正伸向同一扇门。"},"try":{"tw":[["trial",4],["hear",0],["best",3],["act",2],["bring",6],["judge",0],["control",3],["taste",0]],"en":"I will try once more, and then I will stop. The trial next week is about a small house near the river, and the judge has asked me to bring the old papers. We will hear the first witness on Monday. Nothing here is under my control; the best I can do is act quickly and taste the food before I serve it. There is a pain in my back that will not go away. My sister says I should give up, and I tell her that trying is all I have.","zh":"我再试一次，然后就停下。下周的庭审涉及河边一栋小房子，法官要我把旧文件带过去。周一会听第一位证人陈述。这里没有一件事在我掌控之中；我能做的最好的事就是动作快一点，上菜前先尝一口。我背上有一处疼痛怎么也不消。"},"type":{"tw":[["typify",4],["character",0],["breed",3],["write",2],["example",6],["eccentric",0],["shift",3],["adult",2]],"en":"What type of dog is that? The breed is old and rather eccentric: it will typify the whole group in every show. Its character is calm, and the adult dogs sleep all day. I have to write four pages about this type of animal, with an example of each. The night shift begins at ten, and the same man has worked it for years. He says he knows every type by its bark alone. There are forty types in the book, and I have to describe every one of them.","zh":"那是什么品种的狗？这品种很老，也相当古怪：每到比赛它都能代表整组狗的特点。它的性情温和，成年的狗整天睡觉。我得写四页讲这类动物，每一类都要举一个例子。夜班十点开始，同一个人已经干了好几年。他说只听叫声就能认出每一种。"},"use":{"tw":[["usage",4],["employ",0],["apply",0],["drink",3],["demand",2],["require",6],["exercise",0],["board",3],["act",2]],"en":"The use of this room is written on the board. You may employ the machine for two hours a day, but you have to apply in writing first. The usage is strict: no drink near the desk. Older people require a chair and will demand one. We exercise every morning before the doors open, and the act of standing up is the hardest part. Nobody has ever asked me what the machines are for. The man who wrote the rules retired in 1990 and has not been back since. Everyone here knows the rules, and nobody has ever read them.","zh":"这间屋子的用途写在牌子上。你每天可以用这台机器两小时，但得先书面申请。规矩很严：桌边不许喝饮料。年纪大的人需要椅子，而且会开口要。每天早上开门前我们做操，而站起来这个动作是最难的一环。从没有人问过我这些机器是干什么用的。"},"wait":{"tw":[["waiter",4],["expect",3],["extension",3],["act",2],["stay",6],["hold",0],["ambush",3],["look",0]],"en":"We had to wait two hours for a table. The waiter told us to expect another twenty minutes, and then another. My sister could not stay; she had work to do. I left my name at the extension desk and sat in the corner, where I could look at the door. The ambush in the book I was reading lasted three pages. I had to hold the book with both hands, it was so cold. When the table was ready at last, my sister had already gone home. The waiter said the delay was nobody's fault, but every act of service in that place takes an hour.","zh":"我们等位子等了两个小时。服务员说再等二十分钟，然后又二十分钟。我妹妹待不住，她还有活要干。我把名字留在分机台，坐到角落里，从那儿能看见门口。我读的那本书里，一次伏击写了三页。我不得不用两只手抱着书，实在太冷了。"},"wall":{"tw":[["mural",4],["fence",2],["gable",3],["surround",0],["parapet",3],["layer",2],["floor",6],["object",2],["street",6]],"en":"There is a wall around the old garden. On the inside, the mural above the door shows the whole history of the street. The parapet is broken in two places, and a wooden fence covers the gap. Every layer of paint on the wall belongs to a different year. The gable of the house next door leans over it, and on the floor near the gate somebody has left a heavy object. The wall will surround this garden long after we are gone. I sit on the floor by the fence and count the layers of paint with my finger.","zh":"老花园四周有一道墙。墙内侧、门上方那幅壁画讲着这条街的整部历史。墙头有两处塌了，用一道木栅栏挡着缺口。墙上每一层漆都属于不同年份。隔壁房子的山墙朝它倾斜过来，大门附近的地上有人撂下了一个很重的东西。等我们都不在了，这道墙还会围着这座花园。我坐在栅栏边的地上，用手指一层层数那些漆。"},"weight":{"tw":[["weighty",4],["burden",0],["load",3],["charge",2],["maximum",6],["bias",2],["excess",6],["angle",0]],"en":"The weight of the box was more than I expected. It is a weighty thing, and the burden of carrying it up the stairs fell on my brother. The maximum load for the old lift is eighty kilos, so we had to go on foot. He put it on the table at an angle and said the charge would be extra. There is a bias in the way we measure these things: two men always say a box is lighter than one man does. The excess goes back to the yard, where the same two men will argue about the angle of the ramp.","zh":"那个箱子比我想的重。它很沉，搬上楼的担子就落在我哥哥身上。这部旧电梯的最大载重是八十公斤，所以我们只好走楼梯。他把箱子斜着放在桌上，说搬运要另收费。我们衡量这些东西时是有偏见的：两个人总说箱子比一个人说的要轻。"},"simple":{"tw":[["simplicity",4],["bare",0],["square",3],["complex",1],["perfect",6],["mere",0],["fool",3],["straightforward",6]],"en":"The answer is simple. The plan has a kind of simplicity that fools people: a bare room, one square table, one chair. Any honest worker would call it straightforward. The truth is that it is not complex, and it is not perfect either. It is elementary, and only a fool would try to improve it. My father built the whole thing in a single week, and it still stands. For a mere fifty pounds we could make it better, but nobody wants to spend the money. So we leave it as it is, and it works.","zh":"答案很简单。这个方案有一种会骗人的简洁：一间空屋、一张方桌、一把椅子。任何老实的工人都会说这很直白。事实是它不复杂，也不完美。它很基础，只有傻子才会想去改进它。我父亲用一周就把它全做出来了，而它至今还立在那儿。"},"space":{"tw":[["spatial",4],["blank",0],["hole",3],["distance",0],["infinite",0],["shuttle",6],["key",3],["earth",6]],"en":"There is no space left in the cupboard. A hole in the wall behind it gives us a little more, and the distance from there to the window is about a metre. In the city the shuttle bus comes every ten minutes. My teacher says space is infinite and the earth is not, and then he draws a blank on the board. The key to the whole problem is spatial: it is about where things are, not what they are. The hole is blank and the distance looks the same from every angle in the room.","zh":"柜子里没地方了。它后面墙上的一个洞给了我们一点余地，从那儿到窗户的距离大约一米。在城里，穿梭巴士每十分钟一班。我老师说空间是无限的，而地球不是，然后他在黑板上画了个空白。整个问题的关键在于空间：它关乎东西在哪里，而不是它们是什么。那个洞是空的，从屋里每个角度看距离都一样。"},"suppose":{"tw":[["supposition",4],["guess",0],["suspect",3],["assume",2],["premise",3],["presume",6],["imagine",0],["say",0]],"en":"I suppose you have heard the story. It is a supposition, nothing more; nobody can say where it began. I suspect the first man only wanted to make us guess. Do not assume that the premise is true, and do not presume that I know either. Imagine a village where nobody had ever left, and you will understand why the story grew. That is the whole of it. I have told it to my children exactly as it was told to me, without adding anything. They will tell it to theirs, and the supposition will be the same.","zh":"我猜这个故事你听过。它只是一个推测，仅此而已；没人说得出它从哪儿开始。我怀疑最初那个人只是想让我们猜。别认定那个前提是真的，也别以为我就知道。想一想一个从没有人离开过的村子，你就会明白这故事为什么会越传越大。事情就是这样。"},"term":{"tw":[["terminal",4],["condition",0],["subject",3],["word",2],["current",6],["terminus",0],["predicate",3],["quantity",2]],"en":"The term ends in three weeks. In this subject the predicate carries most of the meaning, and one wrong word can change the whole sentence. The quantity of reading is small; the interest is not. I stand at the bus terminal every morning and watch the current of people go past. The line stops at a terminus two streets from my house, and the condition of the road there is terrible. My father uses the same word for the season, the school and the length of a loan. He says a word is only a tool, and a tool should be used more than once.","zh":"学期还有三周就结束了。在这门学科里，谓语承载了大部分意思，一个用错的词就能改变整句。阅读量不大，趣味性却不少。每天早上我站在公交总站看人流经过。这条线路的终点站离我家两条街，而那里路况糟透了。"},"wild":{"tw":[["wilderness",4],["crazy",0],["barren",3],["tame",1],["fish",6],["waste",0],["bird",6],["furious",0]],"en":"The garden has gone wild again. Beyond the fence there is a piece of wilderness where no bird has nested for years and the ground is barren. My neighbour is furious about the waste of good land, and he says only a crazy man would leave it like that. His own cat is tame and fat. I go there to fish in the small stream and to be alone for an hour. In spring the stream is full of small fish and the birds come back to the fence. Nobody in the village has walked to the far end of it for years.","zh":"园子又野了。栅栏那边有一片荒地，多年没有鸟在这里筑巢，土地贫瘠。我邻居对这么好的一块地被浪费感到愤怒，他说只有疯子才会让它这样。他自己那只猫又温顺又肥。我去那里的小溪里钓鱼，独自待上一个小时。"},"sky":{"tw":[["celestial",4],["flip",0],["lag",3],["horizon",6],["fling",2],["pitch",0],["submarine",3],["bright",6],["toss",0]],"en":"On the last night of the trip we lay on the deck and watched the sky. It was bright, with no cloud at all, and a few celestial bodies moved slowly above the horizon. My brother began to toss a coin and flip it, trying to catch it in the dark. Each pitch of the boat made him lag behind the beat of the waves, and once the coin went over the side. A submarine lamp far off threw a pale line on the water. He gave a little fling of his arm and laughed. We stayed out until the sky turned grey.","zh":"旅途的最后一晚，我们躺在甲上看天。天很亮，一丝云也没有，几颗星星慢慢地移过地平线。我弟弟开始抛硬币、翻着玩，想在黑里接住它。船每颠一下，他就比浪的节拍慢半拍，有一次硬币掉进了海里。远处一盏潜水艇的灯在水面上投下一道淡淡的白线。他手臂一甩，笑了。我们在外面待到天色发灰。"},"show":{"tw":[["express",0],["finger",3],["appear",2],["hide",1],["watch",6],["picture",0],["fly",3],["inform",2],["film",6],["present",0]],"en":"The teacher wanted to show us how a moth hides from a bird. She would hold up a picture, then point one finger at the shape on the wall. Watch closely, she said, and you will see it appear and then vanish. She had a short film on an old machine, and she used it to express the same idea in another way. Her aim was to inform, not to amuse us. At the end she asked each of us to present one thing we had learned, and then let a moth fly out of the window.","zh":"老师想让我们看看飞蛾是怎么躲开鸟的。她会举起一张图，再用一根手指点着墙上那个形状。她说：看仔细了，你会看见它先出现，然后又不见。她还有一部旧机器放的短片，就用它把同一个意思换个法子讲了一遍。她的目的是让我们知道些什么，不是逗我们乐。最后她让我们每人讲一件学到的事，然后把一只蛾子从窗口放了出去。"},"side":{"tw":[["face",0],["edge",3],["cut",2],["bottom",3],["rest",6],["position",0],["front",3],["line",2],["back",6],["slope",0]],"en":"Our house stands on the side of a hill, with a steep slope at the front. If you look at its face from the road, you see a line of small windows and a door at the bottom of three steps. On the back side there is a bench where my father likes to rest. He will cut the grass along the edge of the path and then sit down with his back to the wall. From that position he can watch everyone who comes up the road. It is the best seat in the village, he says.","zh":"我们家在山坡上，前面是一道陡坡。你要是从路上看它的门脸，会看到一排小窗，还有三级台阶底下的一扇门。背面有条长凳，我爸喜欢在那儿歇着。他会沿着路边把草剪齐，然后背靠着墙坐下。从那个位置，他看得见每个上坡来的人。他说，这是全村最好的位子。"},"sit":{"tw":[["ride",0],["lounge",3],["serve",2],["lie",1],["wait",6],["seat",0],["perch",3],["travel",2],["stay",6],["model",0]],"en":"On long journeys my aunt would rather sit than lie down. She says that in a lounge car you can watch the country travel past, and that a comfortable seat is worth any amount of money. She used to ride the night train to the coast and perch on a small stool by the window for hours. A waiter would come to serve coffee, and she would stay there until dawn. She has never learned to rest in a bed on a train. I am not a model of good sense, she says, but I do not miss much.","zh":"长途旅行的时候，我姑姑宁可坐着也不肯躺下。她说在休息车厢里能看着乡野往后走，一个舒服的座位值多少钱都行。她从前常坐夜车去海边，一连几个钟头就栖在窗边一张小凳上。服务员会过来送咖啡，她就在那儿一直待到天亮。她始终学不会在火车卧铺上歇着。她说：我不是什么明白人的榜样，但我没漏掉多少东西。"},"slow":{"tw":[["behind",0],["delay",3],["decrease",2],["fast",1],["pace",6],["easy",0],["clog",3],["decelerate",2],["steady",6],["dim",0]],"en":"The traffic was slow all the way out of the city. A single broken lorry had begun to clog the road, and the pace of every car behind it fell to a walk. My father kept a steady voice, but he would not drive fast in the dim light. There is no need to delay anyone, he said, and no harm in being a little behind. When the road opened his worry decreased slowly, and then the speed picked up again. He told me that an easy journey is one where you never have to decelerate suddenly.","zh":"出城的路上一直堵得很慢。一辆坏了的货车把路堵住了，跟在它后面每辆车的速度都降到步行的样子。我爸声音很稳，但天色昏暗他不肯开快。他说：没必要耽误别人，落在后面一点也没什么坏处。路一通，他的担心慢慢消下来，车速也就重新提起来了。他还告诉我，一趟舒服的行程，就是你从来不用猛地减速。"},"start":{"tw":[["begin",2],["birth",3],["act",2],["finish",1],["next",6],["first",0],["fall",3],["leave",2],["break",6],["jump",0]],"en":"The race would start at the first light, and by then the whole village was awake. My cousin had trained all year for it, and he meant to finish in the top ten. At the next bend the road begins to fall away, so the runners have to take it easy or they break their step. I watched him leave the gate and jump the low wall at the corner. It was the birth of something new in him, I think. He said afterwards that the act of starting is the only part that ever frightened him.","zh":"比赛天一亮就开始，到那时候全村人都醒了。我表哥为这场赛跑练了一整年，一心想跑进前十。下一个转弯处路面开始往下斜，所以跑的人得悠着点，不然步子就乱了。我看着他从大门出去，跳过拐角那道矮墙。我觉得，那是他心里有什么新东西生出来了。后来他说，真正让他害怕的只有起跑那一下。"},"stop":{"tw":[["bar",0],["call",3],["act",2],["start",1],["move",6],["break",3],["close",3],["stay",2],["prevent",6],["catch",2]],"en":"The bus makes one stop at the end of our road, and if you do not catch it there you must walk. The driver will call out the name of the place and then close the doors. There is a metal bar across the front window, and a small sign that says you must not stay on after the last stop of the day. In winter the ice can prevent the bus from moving at all, and then my mother has to act quickly and find another way to get to work. The rain began to break just as we started out.","zh":"公共汽车在我们这条路尽头有一站，要是在那儿没赶上，就只能走路了。司机报出地名，然后关门。前窗上横着一根金属杆，还有块小牌子写着：到当天最后一站后不得继续留在车上。冬天结冰能让车根本动不了，那时候我妈就得赶紧想办法，另外找路去上班。我们刚出发，雨就开始小下来了。"},"tail":{"tw":[["behind",0],["tree",3],["cut",2],["head",1],["nose",6],["bottom",0],["brush",3],["end",2],["snout",6],["dog",0]],"en":"My dog will run in circles and chase his own tail until he falls over. He is a small thing with a black nose and a wet snout, and he keeps his head down when he is working. At the bottom of the garden there is an old tree, and he likes to sit behind it. I have to brush him every week and cut the hair that grows long at the end of his back. He watches me with his tail still, waiting for the brush to come near him again.","zh":"我的狗会绕着圈跑，追自己的尾巴，一直追到摔倒。它个头小，黑鼻子，鼻头总是湿的，干活的时候脑袋低着。园子尽头有一棵老树，它喜欢坐在树后面。我每个星期都得给它刷毛，把脊背末端长出来的毛剪掉。它尾巴一动不动地盯着我，等刷子再靠近它。"},"top":{"tw":[["clear",0],["head",3],["complete",2],["bottom",1],["key",6],["cover",0],["tail",3],["degree",2],["hold",6],["lead",0]],"en":"We climbed to the top of the hill on a clear morning. My brother held the key to the gate in his hand and would not let go of it. At the bottom of the slope a road led away to the next town, and above our heads the cover of cloud began to lift. A dog ran past us with its tail up, and we watched it go. He wanted to complete the walk before noon, so we had to hold a good speed. It was, to a high degree, the best morning of that whole year.","zh":"一个晴朗的早晨，我们爬到了山顶。我弟弟手里攥着大门的钥匙，怎么都不肯放。坡底下有条路通向邻镇，我们头顶上的云层开始散开。一条狗翘着尾巴从我们身边跑过，我们看着它跑远。他想在中午前走完这趟，所以我们得保持一个不错的速度。那真是那一年里最好的一个早晨，好得没法说。"},"wake":{"tw":[["heat",0],["call",3],["change",2],["sleep",1],["fall",6],["awake",0],["ferment",3],["island",2],["fear",6],["arouse",0]],"en":"The heat would wake me before six every morning that summer, and I would lie still and try to sleep again. My father would call from the yard, then fall quiet, waiting for me to come down. On the island there was nothing to fear and nothing to hurry for. The change came slowly: by August I was awake at five without any noise at all, and I began to ferment ideas about what I would do when we went home. He could arouse me with a single word. Years later I still wake at that hour, and the old house comes back to me in the dark.","zh":"那年夏天，每天早上六点不到，热气就把我叫醒了，我就躺着不动，想再睡一会儿。我爸会在院子里喊我，然后安静下来，等我下楼。在岛上没什么可怕的，也没什么要赶的。变化是慢慢来的：到了八月，我五点就醒，一点动静都不用，脑子里开始发酵起回家以后要干什么的念头。他一个字就能把我叫起来。很多年以后我还是那个点醒，那栋老房子就在黑里回到我眼前。"},"waste":{"tw":[["blow",0],["burn",3],["act",2],["conserve",1],["water",6],["wild",0],["rubbish",3],["kill",2],["garbage",6],["rot",0]],"en":"It is a waste to burn good wood in an open fire, and my father would not act so foolishly. He told us to conserve what we had and never to let food rot in the box. The wild part of the garden was full of rubbish and old garbage, and he made us clear it every spring. If a storm should blow down a tree, we had to cut it up that week or the water would get in and kill the wood. He said a house that lets things go is a house that is already lost.","zh":"在明火上烧好木头是浪费，我爸不会干这种蠢事。他叫我们省着用手里有的，别让吃食在箱子里烂掉。园子荒着的那半边净是垃圾和烂七八糟的旧东西，他每年春天都逼我们去清一遍。要是风把树刮倒了，我们得在那个星期里把它锯开，不然水汽钻进去，木头就废了。他说，一栋什么都撒手不管的房子，其实早就没了。"},"wind":{"tw":[["lead",0],["ball",3],["move",2],["unwind",1],["rain",6],["lift",0],["clue",3],["raise",2],["water",6],["nose",0]],"en":"The wind came up the valley just before the rain started. My uncle had to lead the boat round, and my job was to raise the sail and keep the nose of it into the weather. There was no clue where the storm would move next. A ball of grey cloud sat on the hills and would not lift. When it was over I would unwind the wet rope and hang it on the fence. Over the water afterwards there was a fine line of foam as far as I could see.","zh":"雨还没下，风就先顺着山谷上来了。我叔得把船领回去，我的活儿是把帆升起来，让船头迎着风。谁也说不准风暴接下来往哪儿挪。山上蹲着一团灰云，怎么也不肯散。事后我把湿绳子解开绕松，挂在栅栏上。那之后水面上拉着一条细白的泡沫，一眼望不到头。"},"song":{"tw":[["sing",4],["strain",0],["carol",3],["sound",2],["pop",6],["vocal",0],["anthem",3],["tune",6]],"en":"My aunt could sing anything, from a carol at Christmas to a pop song on the radio. She had a strong vocal line and could hold a tune for a whole verse without effort. When the old anthem was played at the village meeting, she stood up and the sound of her voice filled the hall. She said she had learned it all by ear, and that a strain of music heard once was enough for her. She never sang for money. At the end of the evening the whole room would ask her for one more, and she always gave it.","zh":"我姑姑什么都能唱，从圣诞的颂歌到收音机里流行的曲子。她嗓子很稳，一整段调子不用费劲就能托住。村里聚会上放那首老颂歌的时候，她站起来，她的声音把整个礼堂都填满了。她说她全是听会的，一段曲子只要听过一遍就够她用了。她从不为钱唱。晚上快结束时，满屋的人都会再要一首，她从来没推过。"},"tend":{"tw":[["tender",4],["run",0],["garden",3],["attend",2],["alike",6],["lean",0],["suffer",3],["incline",0]],"en":"My grandmother used to tend the garden in the mornings, before anyone else was up. She would lean on her stick to reach the far bed, and she had a tender way with young plants that I have never been able to copy. She had to attend to the roses first, then run a hose along the wall. She said that all living things are alike in this: they suffer when they are forgotten. I incline to think she was right. In July the garden gave back more than she could eat, and she would leave boxes of it at the gate.","zh":"我奶奶从前每天早上都照料园子，比别人起得都早。她会撑着棍子去够最远那畦，对嫩苗那份轻柔劲儿，我怎么学也学不来。她得先照看玫瑰，再顺墙拉一条水管浇水。她说所有活物在这一点上都一样：没人管，就受苦。我也倾向认为她是对的。到了七月，园子里长出来的东西她根本吃不完，就把一箱箱菜放在大门口。"},"will":{"tw":[["willing",4],["leave",0],["remember",3],["decide",2],["testament",0],["devise",3],["purpose",2],["bequeath",0]],"en":"My great-uncle was a man of strong will and few words. He was willing to help anyone, but he would not be told what to do. When he could no longer leave the house, he decided to write his testament himself, and he would remember every cousin by name. He devised a simple plan: the land to his son, the tools to the man who had worked for him longest. He said his purpose was only to avoid a quarrel after he was gone. He would bequeath nothing that could be argued over.","zh":"我叔公是个意志很硬、话很少的人。他愿意帮任何人的忙，但谁也别想指挥他。到出不了门的时候，他决定自己写遗嘱，还把每个表亲的名字都记得清清楚楚。他定了个简单的方案：地给儿子，工具给跟他干得最久的那个伙计。他说他的用意只是免得自己走以后有人吵架。凡是可能被人争的东西，他一件都不留。"},"sleep":{"tw":[["rest",2],["bundle",3],["accommodate",2],["wake",1],["pain",6],["nap",3],["hibernate",3],["awake",6],["slumber",0]],"en":"My grandfather could sleep anywhere, at any hour, and he would take a nap sitting up. The house had to accommodate nine people, so he would roll himself in a bundle of coats and lie down in the corner. He would never wake before six, even when the pain in his back was bad. In winter he slept like something that hibernates, and we would not disturb him for any reason. My grandmother used to say that sleep was his rest and his medicine both. I do not think he was ever fully awake before noon. His slumber was the deepest I have ever known.","zh":"我爷爷在哪儿都能睡，什么钟点都能睡，还能坐着打盹。那屋子得住九个人，他就把自己裹进一摞外套里，往墙角一躺。他总是六点前不醒，哪怕背疼得厉害。冬天他睡得像个冬眠的东西，我们有什么事都不去吵他。奶奶常说，睡觉对他既是休息也是药。我看他中午以前就没完全醒过。他那种沉睡，是我见过最深的。"},"slip":{"tw":[["mistake",2],["lead",3],["forget",2],["bounce",6],["steal",0],["stay",3],["move",2],["knock",6],["trip",0]],"en":"I made one slip on the wet step, and the whole tray went over. It was a small mistake, but it led to three days of cleaning. I did not want to forget how it felt, so I wrote the date on the wall of the yard. A ball would bounce against that wall all afternoon. Somebody had tried to steal the milk twice that month, and my mother would not stay quiet about it. She would move the box inside every night and knock the ice off the step. After my trip on the ice, she bought a mat. I still watch that step.","zh":"我在湿台阶上滑了一跤，整盘东西都翻了。这错不大，可害我收拾了三天。我不想忘了那种滋味，就把日子写在院墙上。整个下午都有球往那面墙上弹。那个月有人两次想偷牛奶，母亲不肯把这事忍着不说。她每天夜里把箱子搬进屋，再把台阶上的冰敲掉。我在冰上绊那一回之后，她买了块垫子。那个台阶我现在还会多看一眼。"},"smell":{"tw":[["feel",0],["nose",3],["suggest",2],["smoke",6],["look",0],["scent",3],["atmosphere",2],["stench",6],["sense",0]],"en":"When I opened the kitchen door, the smell of smoke met me at once. My nose knew something was wrong before my eyes did, and the whole room had a heavy atmosphere. I could feel the heat from the old stove. A thin line of smoke rose from a pan, and the stench grew worse every second. I looked under the pan and found a black mark. That would suggest the wires had burned. I lost all sense of time and just stood there. Some sweet scent from yesterday's bread still hung in the air, which made the moment even stranger.","zh":"我推开厨房门，一股烟味马上扑过来。眼睛还没看见，鼻子就已经知道出了事，整间屋子都弥漫着一股沉闷的气息。我能感觉到那台旧炉子的热气。一缕烟从锅里升起来，臭味一秒比一秒重。我往锅底下看，发现一块黑色的印子。那说明电线已经烧了。我一时没了时间感，只是呆站着。昨天剩下的面包的甜香还飘在空气里，让这一刻更古怪。"},"smoke":{"tw":[["pot",0],["cigarette",3],["pitch",2],["dust",6],["weed",0],["inhale",3],["consume",2],["smell",6],["fume",0]],"en":"My uncle spent the morning burning dry weed in the back yard. Thick smoke rose from the pile and hung above the fence. He said the fumes would keep the insects away. I helped him carry the old pot and watched the dust settle on everything. He lit a cigarette and stood there, watching the fire eat the wood. The smoke was black as pitch. I had to hold my breath, because every time I tried to inhale, my throat hurt. The smell stayed on my coat for days, and the fire seemed to consume the whole pile before noon.","zh":"我叔一上午都在后院烧干草。浓烟从草堆上升起来，挂在篱笆上方。他说这些烟能把虫子赶走。我帮他搬来那只旧锅，看着灰尘落在所有东西上。他点了根烟站着，看火一点点吃掉木头。烟黑得像沥青。我只好屏住呼吸，因为每次想吸气，喉咙就疼。那股味儿在我外套上留了好几天，火到中午前像是把整堆都吞掉了。"},"sort":{"tw":[["class",0],["count",3],["choose",2],["mind",6],["form",0],["like",3],["category",2],["sense",6],["screen",0]],"en":"On Saturday my sister helped sort books at the charity shop. The manager asked her to count every box first and then choose a place for each one. In her mind, the books fell into two groups: those people would like, and those nobody would touch. She had to form a clear plan. Each class of book went to its own shelf, and every category had a small sign. She used an old screen to check the covers for damage. It made good sense to keep the children's books low, where small hands could reach them. By five, the whole shop looked new.","zh":"周六我妹妹去慈善商店帮忙整理书。店长让她先把每个箱子数一遍，再给每本书挑个位置。在她心里，书分成两类：人们会喜欢的，和谁都不碰的。她得理出一个清楚的计划。每一类书各上自己的架，每个类别都配个小牌子。她用一块旧筛板检查封面有没有破损。把童书放低、让小手够得着，这很合理。到五点，整家店看着像新的。"},"spot":{"tw":[["bit",0],["end",3],["change",2],["bottom",6],["position",0],["high",3],["dirty",2],["straight",6],["post",0]],"en":"We walked until we found a quiet spot at the end of the lake, just past a wooden post. From that high position we could see the whole valley. My boots were dirty from the long path, and there was a small bit of mud on my coat. I put the map straight on the ground and sat down. The place had not changed much since our last visit. At the bottom of the hill, the water was almost still. It was a good spot for lunch. Then a cold wind came, and we knew it was time to move on.","zh":"我们一直走到湖的尽头，才找到一处安静的落脚点，就在一根木桩过去一点。站上那个高处，整个山谷都看得见。走了这么长的路，我的靴子脏了，外套上也有一小点泥。我把地图直接摊在地上，坐了下来。这地方跟上次来比没什么变化。山脚下，水面几乎不动。在这儿吃午饭挺好。后来起了冷风，我们就知道该走了。"},"spring":{"tw":[["form",0],["burst",3],["grow",2],["summer",6],["jump",2],["hop",3],["move",2],["winter",6],["bounce",3]],"en":"In spring the garden began to grow again, and my little sister could not sit still. She would jump on the old sofa, whose springs had lost their form years ago, and every hop sent her a little higher. I told her to bounce gently, but she would not move. All summer she practised, and by winter she could land on her feet. One cold morning the old spring burst through the cloth and cut the seat. She cried for a minute, then said it was only cloth, and asked when we could buy a new one before next spring.","zh":"春天一到，园子又开始生长，我妹妹坐不住。她在那张旧沙发上蹦，沙发的弹簧早没了形，每跳一下都把她弹得高一点。我叫她轻点弹，她就是不肯挪窝。整个夏天她都在练，到冬天已经能稳稳落地。一个冷早上，那根旧弹簧顶破布面，把坐垫划开了。她哭了一分钟，然后说不过是块布罢了，还问我们能不能在明年春天前买个新的。"},"square":{"tw":[["straight",0],["plaza",3],["position",2],["round",1],["around",6],["feather",0],["settle",2],["gate",6],["solid",0]],"en":"The old plaza had a small square of grass in the middle, and a low gate at each corner. I stood in one position and looked straight across it. A white feather drifted through the air, went round once, and then began to settle on the ground. Around the square, people walked slowly in the evening light. The stone under my feet felt solid and cold. Nothing moved except the feather. I thought of all the feet that had crossed this ground before mine. I waited a long time, and at last it came to rest at the edge of the grass.","zh":"那座老广场中央有一小块方形草地，四个角各有一道矮门。我站在一个位置上，笔直地望过去。一根白羽毛在空中飘着，转了一圈，慢慢落向地面。广场四周，人们在暮色里慢慢走着。脚下的石头又硬又凉。除了那根羽毛，什么也没动。我想起在我之前有多少双脚踩过这片地。我等了很久，它最后停在草地边上。"},"stay":{"tw":[["check",2],["stand",3],["act",2],["change",1],["leave",6],["continue",0],["meet",2],["wait",6],["rest",0]],"en":"I had to check in at the small hotel and then decide whether to stay the night. The woman behind the desk did not act surprised when I asked for a quiet room. I said I would wait, and had to stand by the window while she looked for a key. Outside, the rain had started, and that made the choice easier. Then she said the price would not change, so I could stay as long as I liked. I had planned to meet a friend, but I was too tired. I decided to leave it till morning and continue my journey after a good rest.","zh":"我得先在小旅馆办入住，再决定要不要住一晚。我说想要个安静的房间，柜台后的女人一点不显得意外。我说我等，就站在窗边，看她找钥匙。外面下起了雨，这让选择容易了些。她说价钱不会变，我想住多久都行。我本来打算见个朋友，可实在累了。我决定推到早上，好好歇一晚再继续赶路。"},"steal":{"tw":[["buy",0],["hook",3],["move",2],["grab",6],["slip",0],["pocket",3],["gain",2],["retrieve",6],["bargain",0]],"en":"At the market my cousin tried to steal a small silver hook from a table. He did not want to buy it; he only wanted the gain. I watched his hand move toward it and grab the edge of the cloth. A coin began to slip from his pocket and fell on the ground. The old woman turned and saw him. He tried to retrieve it, but she had already picked it up. We had to bargain hard before she let us leave. In the end we paid for it, and I told him never to try that again.","zh":"在集市上，我表弟想从一张桌子上偷一个小银钩。他不是想买，只想占那个便宜。我看着他的手朝它伸过去，抓住布边。一枚硬币开始从他口袋里滑出来，掉在地上。老妇人转过身看见了他。他想把它捡回去，可她已经先拿在手里了。我们费了好大劲讨价还价，她才放我们走。最后我们付了钱，我告诉他以后再也别干这种事。"},"step":{"tw":[["measure",0],["cut",3],["mark",2],["push",6],["tone",0],["trip",3],["move",2],["change",6],["abuse",0]],"en":"The carpenter took one step back and looked at the board again. The old shop was quiet except for the saw. He had to measure it twice before he could cut it clean. With a pencil he made a small mark near the end. His tone was quiet, but he did not like to be pushed. If anyone rushed him, he would stop and say there was no need for abuse. A single wrong move could ruin the whole piece. Nothing would change his way of working. As he lifted the wood, he nearly tripped over a box on the floor.","zh":"木匠往后退了一步，又看了看那块木板。这间旧作坊里除了锯子声，静得很。他量了两遍才下刀，切得利落。他用铅笔在末端画了个小记号。他语气很轻，但不喜欢被人催。谁要是催他，他就停下来说用不着那样数落人。一个动作做错，整块料就毁了。没什么能改他的做法。他抬木头时，差点被地上的箱子绊倒。"},"stick":{"tw":[["beat",0],["club",3],["force",2],["loose",6],["stay",0],["bow",3],["leg",2],["right",6],["bind",3]],"en":"In the garden my grandfather used a straight stick to hold up a young tree. He would bind it with a soft rope, but not too tight, and leave the knot loose. When the wind was strong, the tree had to stay upright, so he pushed the stick deep into the soil. He had to use some force, because the ground was hard. His dog lay at his right leg and watched. If the dog came too close, he would gently beat the grass with a small club. Then he would bow his head and check the rope once more.","zh":"在园子里，我爷爷用一根直木棍撑住一棵小树。他用软绳把它绑起来，但不绑太紧，结留得松松的。风大的时候树得立住，所以他把木棍深深插进土里。他得使点劲，因为地很硬。他的狗趴在他右腿边看着。狗要是靠太近，他就用小木棒轻轻打一下草。然后他低下头，又检查了一遍绳子。"},"still":{"tw":[["however",0],["compose",3],["change",2],["though",6],["quiet",5],["gag",3],["comfort",2],["once",6],["calm",5]],"en":"The house was still at last, and the night air felt calm and cool. My mother sat by the lamp to compose a long letter. She said the quiet was a comfort after such a busy week. However, she did not stay calm for long. Once the phone rang, she had to stop. Though she tried to keep her tone even, I could hear that something had changed. She made a small gag about her own memory, and we both laughed. I felt the day fall away from me. Then she went back to her page, and the room grew still again.","zh":"屋里终于静下来了，夜里的空气又凉又平和。我妈坐在灯边写一封长信。她说忙了一周，这份安静是种安慰。可她没能安静多久。电话一响，她就得停下。虽然她努力把语气放平，我还是听出有什么变了。她拿自己的记性开了个小玩笑，我们俩都笑了。我觉得这一天的疲惫都落了下去。然后她又回到那页纸上，屋里重新静了下来。"},"stone":{"tw":[["rock",0],["crystal",3],["kill",2],["wood",6],["pit",0],["gravel",3],["material",2],["brick",6],["gem",0]],"en":"My father was digging a pit in the yard when his spade hit a large stone. He set the rock aside and looked at it. The soil around it was dry and hard. It was heavy and grey, the same material as the wall behind him. He had built that wall himself, brick by brick, and mixed the gravel with his own hands. Under the stone he found a small crystal that shone like a gem. He said it was not worth much, but it would not kill anyone to keep it. Beside it lay a piece of old wood, black with age.","zh":"我爸在院子里挖坑，铁锹碰到一块大石头。他把那块石头挪到一边看。周围的土又干又硬。它又重又灰，和他身后那堵墙是同一种料。那墙是他自己一块砖一块砖砌的，沙砾也是他亲手和的。石头下面，他发现一小块水晶，亮得像宝石。他说这不值多少钱，可留着也不碍事。旁边还躺着一块旧木头，黑得发陈。"},"strike":{"tw":[["discover",0],["beat",3],["blow",2],["halt",6],["fall",0],["bottom",3],["find",2],["break",6],["hit",0]],"en":"A heavy storm was about to strike the small town, and the workers had to halt their work at the old factory. They had already planned a strike for better pay, and now the weather made things worse. The first blow of wind came at noon. It was strong enough to beat against the windows and break a branch off the tree. I ran to find my father at the bottom of the yard. A stone fell and hit the roof. My mother called us in, but nobody moved. That night we would discover that the whole wall had begun to crack.","zh":"一场大雨要打向小镇，老工厂的工人只好停下手里的活。他们本来就打算罢工要求加钱，现在天气又添了乱。正午刮来第一阵风，猛烈得拍打窗户，还吹断了一根树枝。我跑去院子最里头找我爸。一块石头掉下来砸在屋顶上。我妈喊我们进屋，可谁也没动。那天晚上我们才发现，整堵墙已经开始裂了。"},"stuff":{"tw":[["block",0],["paper",3],["fill",2],["fun",6],["material",0],["waste",3],["push",2],["maybe",6],["shove",0]],"en":"The garage was full of stuff nobody had used for years. My brother and I had to block the door and sort it into piles. There were boxes of old paper, and a great deal of waste we could not keep. The whole job was not much fun. We would push one heavy box, then shove another out to the road. Maybe, I said, we should just leave it all. By noon the space was clear, and we used the last box to fill the gap under the shelf. My mother said the whole material would go to the recycling van.","zh":"车库里堆满了多少年没人用的东西。我和弟弟只好把门堵上，一点点分成堆。有几箱旧纸张，还有一大堆留不得的废品。这活儿一点不好玩。我们推走一个沉箱子，又把另一个搡到路边。我说，也许干脆全扔了算了。到中午，地方空出来了，我们用最后一个箱子填上架子下面的空当。我妈说这些材料都要给回收车拉走。"},"subject":{"tw":[["field",0],["major",3],["term",2],["context",6],["issue",0],["question",3],["affect",2],["instance",6],["matter",0]],"en":"In my first term at college I had to choose a main subject. My teacher said the choice would affect the rest of my life, which I thought was too much to say. I liked history best, because it is a field where every small issue has a context. She asked me a simple question: what do I want to do with it? For instance, I could study law, or teach. She told me there was no need to hurry. It did not matter how long I took. In the end I picked history as my major, and I have never been sorry.","zh":"上大学的第一个学期，我得选一门主修科目。老师说这个选择会影响我一辈子，我觉得这话说得太满了。我最喜欢历史，因为在这个领域里，每个小问题都有自己的来龙去脉。她问了我一个简单的问题：我打算拿它做什么？比如，我可以学法律，也可以去教书。她说不用着急。最后我选了历史作主修，从没后悔过。"},"suit":{"tw":[["cause",0],["agree",3],["meet",2],["complaint",6],["fit",0],["trump",3],["match",2],["white",6],["accommodate",0]],"en":"At the club we would meet every Friday to play cards in the back room. My uncle always wore the same old suit, grey and worn, and a white shirt that no longer fit him well. He would never agree to change it. He liked to hold his cards close and wait for a good match. When he finally played a trump, the whole table went quiet. His only complaint was that the room could not accommodate so many players. Nobody could cause him to hurry. He said a good suit of cards, like a good suit of clothes, needs patience.","zh":"在俱乐部，我们每周五都在里屋碰头打牌。我叔总穿着同一套旧西装，灰扑扑的，还有件早就不合身的白衬衫。他从不答应换。他喜欢把牌捏得紧紧的，等一手好牌。等他一甩出王牌，整张桌子都安静了。他唯一的抱怨是这屋子坐不下这么多人。谁也催不动他。他说一副好牌跟一套好衣服一样，都得有耐心。"},"support":{"tw":[["back",3],["accept",3],["act",2],["aim",6],["bear",0],["carry",3],["agree",2],["maintain",6],["hold",0]],"en":"The old bridge could no longer hold the weight of the trucks, and the town had to act fast. My father worked there for a month, helping to build new support under each end. His aim was simple: to make it safe again. He would carry heavy beams and bear the cold wind without a word. At home, my mother had to maintain the house alone, and my back began to ache from the work. In the end we all had to accept that we could not agree on everything. People came from far away to see it. The new bridge opened in spring.","zh":"那座老桥再也撑不住卡车的重量，镇上必须赶快动手。我爸在那儿干了一个月，帮着在两头重建支撑。他的目的很简单：让它重新变结实。他扛起重梁，顶着冷风一句怨言也没有。在家里，我妈得一个人撑着这个家，我的背也开始因为干活而酸痛。最后我们都得接受，不可能事事都意见一致。人们从老远赶来看新桥。新桥在春天通了。"},"table":{"tw":[["board",0],["call",3],["arrange",2],["sit",6],["defer",0],["hold",3],["delay",2],["open",6],["postpone",0]],"en":"The board was going to meet at the long table on Monday, but the manager had to postpone it. He said he would call each member and arrange a new time. I had to sit in the empty room while he made his calls. The delay was not his fault; the figures were not ready. He decided to defer the whole thing until the numbers were checked. I wrote a short note on the table and left it there. On Tuesday he called again to say the meeting would hold on Friday, and the room would open at nine.","zh":"董事会本来周一要在那张长桌边开会，可经理不得不推迟。他说会挨个打电话通知大家，另约时间。他打电话的时候，我只能坐在空屋里等。这次拖延不怪他，数字还没弄好。他决定等数字核对完再谈整件事。我在桌上写了张短条留在那儿。周二他又打来电话，说会议改在周五开，房间九点开门。"},"talk":{"tw":[["mouth",0],["continue",3],["address",2],["why",6],["sing",3],["shout",3],["conversation",2],["call",6],["speak",0]],"en":"The old teacher gave a talk about the river to a room of students. She did not shout, and she never had to call for quiet. When she opened her mouth, everyone listened. She would speak slowly and then continue, as if she had all night. Her address was simple and warm, and it held our attention to the end. I did not want that hour to end, and I took notes all the way through. Afterwards a girl asked why the water had changed colour. That short conversation stayed with me for years. Sometimes, walking home, I still hear her speak, and I could sing her words like a song.","zh":"那位老教师在一屋子学生面前做了一场关于这条河的演讲。她不喊，也从不用叫大家安静。她一开口，所有人都听着。她慢慢讲，接着往下说，好像有一整夜的时间。她的话朴素又温和，一直把我们吸引到最后。我舍不得那一小时结束，从头到尾都在记笔记。散场后一个女孩问，为什么河水变了颜色。那段短短的交谈我记了好多年。有时回家的路上，我还能听见她说话，真想把她的话像歌一样唱出来。"},"taste":{"tw":[["try",0],["finish",3],["experience",2],["mix",6],["sample",0],["sweet",3],["know",2],["blend",6],["smack",0]],"en":"My aunt let me try her soup before dinner. I had to sample it twice, because the first taste was too sweet. She wanted to know if the blend was right, so she mixed in a little salt and let me taste again. It was not the taste I expected, and for a moment I did not know what to say. I had never had that experience before. She said cooking was like this: you have to finish slowly and trust your own mouth. When the soup was right, she would smack her lips and smile. The whole kitchen smelled of herbs.","zh":"晚饭前，我姑姑让我尝尝她的汤。我得尝两遍，因为第一口的味道太甜了。她想知道混得对不对，就加了一点点盐，又让我尝。这味道和我预想的不一样，有那么一会儿我不知道该说什么。这种体验我以前从没有过。她说做菜就是这样：得慢慢收尾，还要信自己的嘴。汤对味了，她就咂咂嘴笑一下。整间厨房都是香草味。"},"tear":{"tw":[["charge",0],["shred",3],["cry",2],["riot",6],["pull",0],["cleave",3],["drop",2],["disperse",6],["rent",3]],"en":"The news said there had been a riot in the town square, and the police had to charge into the crowd. People began to disperse along the side streets, and some ran past our gate. My mother sat by the window and started to cry. She held an old letter and began to pull at it, as if she wanted to shred it or cleave it in two. A single tear made a drop on the paper. Then she tore it clean, and the rent showed a name she had tried to forget. I did not ask her about the name. The crowd was gone by dark.","zh":"新闻说镇广场上出了乱子，警察不得不冲进人群。人们沿着小巷四散开，有人从我们家门口跑过。我妈坐在窗边，哭了起来。她拿着一封旧信，开始拉扯，像是要把它撕碎，或者干脆掰成两半。一滴眼泪落在纸上。然后她把它撕开，那道口子里露出一个她想忘掉的名字。我没问她那是谁。天黑前，人群散了。"},"test":{"tw":[["run",0],["control",3],["check",2],["final",6],["try",0],["float",3],["attempt",2],["match",6],["exam",0]],"en":"On the day of the final exam, my hands would not stay still. I had made one last attempt to check my notes the night before. The teacher said we could not run out of time if we worked steadily. Halfway through, I lost control of my pen and dropped it. I had to try again from the top of the page. Later, at the pond, we put my small boat in the water to see if it would float. It did not sink, and it did not match the design in my book, but it was a good test.","zh":"期末考试那天，我的手一直静不下来。前一晚我还做了最后一次尝试，把笔记对了一遍。老师说只要稳稳地做，时间就不会不够。做到一半，我握不住笔，把它掉在了地上。我只好从这页的最上面重新来。后来在池塘边，我们把我的小船放进水里，看它能不能浮起来。它没沉，虽然和我书上画的样子不太一样，但这算是一次不错的试验。"},"think":{"tw":[["consider",0],["feel",3],["change",2],["why",6],["guess",0],["hold",3],["concentrate",2],["sure",6],["imagine",2]],"en":"I sat on the step and tried to think about the offer. I had to consider what I would lose if I left my old job. My mother said I should hold on a little longer and not change too fast. I could not guess what the manager really wanted. When I tried to concentrate, my mind went blank. I began to imagine a small flat in another town, with a window I could open. The evening light made everything look far away. I was not sure about anything. I asked myself why I felt so afraid of a simple choice.","zh":"我坐在台阶上，想好好琢磨那份工作机会。我得想清楚，辞掉旧工作会失去什么。我妈说再撑一撑，别换得太急。我猜不透经理到底要什么。想集中精神的时候，脑子却一片空白。我开始想象另一座城里的一间小公寓，有一扇能推开的窗户。暮色让一切都显得很远。我什么都不确定。我问自己，为什么一个简单的选择会让我这么怕。"},"throw":{"tw":[["drop",0],["ground",3],["express",2],["grab",6],["hold",0],["pass",3],["move",2],["ball",6],["cast",0]],"en":"In the yard the boys would throw a worn ball to each other until the light went. My little brother could not hold it long; he would drop it, then grab it again from the ground. He wanted to express how fast he could move, so he ran around us in a circle. When I tried to pass the ball to him, he missed. It was only a game, so we both laughed. On his next try he would cast it so high that we had to run after it. Our father said a good throw comes from the whole body, not just the arm.","zh":"院子里，男孩们会把一个旧球互相扔来扔去，直到天光暗下来。我弟弟抱不了多久，球会掉下去，他再从地上捡起来。他想让人看看自己跑得多快，就绕着我们跑了一圈。我想把球传给他，他接丢了。这本来就是个玩，我们俩都笑了。下一回他把球扔得老高，我们只好追着跑。我爸说，好的一投靠的是整个身子，不只是手臂。"},"tire":{"tw":[["wear",0],["retire",3],["consume",2],["refresh",1],["brake",6],["exhaust",3],["devolve",2],["wheel",6],["weary",0]],"en":"On the long drive home, one front tire began to wear thin, and the car started to pull to the side. My father had to brake slowly and stop by the road. He was too weary to change the wheel himself, and the heat would exhaust him further. He said the journey had begun to consume his strength. His plan was to retire early that year, and now he wished he had. We found a small garage where the work devolved to a young mechanic, who put on a spare. A short rest seemed to refresh my father, and by dusk we were moving again.","zh":"开车回家的长途上，一只前胎越来越薄，车开始往一边偏。我爸只好慢慢刹车，停在路边。他太累了，自己换不动轮子，天热又让他更乏。他说这趟路开始耗他的力气。他本来就打算那年早点退休，这时真希望自己已经退了。我们找到一家小修理铺，活儿落到一个年轻师傅手里，他装上了备胎。歇了这一小会儿，我爸像是缓过来了，天擦黑时我们又上路了。"},"track":{"tw":[["course",0],["drive",3],["bar",2],["speed",6],["cover",0],["round",3],["line",2],["tour",6],["cross",0]],"en":"The old track beside the river had been laid for a small train, but now people used it for a race. My uncle would drive us there and wait by the wooden bar at the gate. The riders had to cover three rounds before the finish, and their speed was hard to believe. Each one kept to his own line. A guide gave us a short tour of the sheds before the start. The dust they raised hung over the path. We watched them cross the far end of the course, then come back toward us in a wide curve.","zh":"河边那条旧轨道原本是给一列小火车铺的，如今人们拿它来赛跑。我叔会开车带我们去，在门口的横木边等着。骑手们要跑完三圈才算完，他们的速度快得让人不敢信。每个人都守着自己那条线。开赛前，一个向导带我们简短地看了看那些棚子。他们扬起的尘土飘在小路上。我们看着他们冲过赛道那头，又划着一道大弯朝我们回来。"},"train":{"tw":[["check",0],["charge",3],["control",2],["taxi",6],["educate",2],["hold",3],["position",2],["traffic",6],["prepare",0]],"en":"We had to check the time before we left for the station, because the train would not wait. My mother called a taxi, and we sat in heavy traffic all the way across town. She could not control her worry. At the gate a woman in a uniform began to charge each passenger for the bags. We had to hold our tickets in our hands and prepare for the rush. The train stood in its usual position on the far platform. We reached the platform just in time. I used the long ride to educate myself about the city from the window.","zh":"出发前我们得先核对时间，因为火车不会等人。我妈叫了辆出租车，我们从城这头到那头一路堵着。她管不住自己的担心。检票口有个穿制服的女人开始按行李向每位乘客收费。我们只好把票攥在手里，为那阵拥挤做准备。火车就停在远处站台上它一贯的位置。我们及时赶到了站台。我一路上都在透过车窗让自己多了解这座城市。"},"treat":{"tw":[["address",0],["feed",3],["affect",2],["patient",6],["cover",0],["nurse",3],["provide",2],["pain",6],["deal",0]],"en":"The nurse had to treat an old patient whose pain had grown worse all week. She would feed him slowly and then cover him with a thin blanket. His illness had begun to affect his mood, and he did not like to deal with strangers. She knew his address by heart, though she had never been to his house. The hospital could not provide a private room, so he stayed in the ward. She told him she would treat him like her own father. One small kindness was enough for the day. He said she was the only one who had time for him.","zh":"那位护士要照料一位老病人，他疼了整整一周，越来越重。她会慢慢喂他吃饭，再给他盖上一床薄毯。病痛开始影响他的情绪，他也不喜欢跟生人打交道。她牢牢记着他的住址，虽然从没去过他家。医院腾不出单人病房，他就住在普通病房里。她对他说，会像照顾自己的父亲一样照料他。这一天，一点点善意就够了。他说，只有她还肯为他花时间。"},"trip":{"tw":[["slip",0],["run",3],["catch",2],["visit",6],["travel",3],["flight",3],["experience",2],["journey",6],["trigger",0]],"en":"Last summer we took a long trip to the coast. The flight was short, but the journey from the airport took hours. My sister had to run to catch the last bus and nearly made me slip on the wet steps. We planned to visit an old town the next morning. That was the experience I remember best: narrow streets, low doors, and a warm wind from the sea. Nothing seemed able to trigger a bad mood that week. Even when it began to rain, we only travelled more slowly and laughed about it. We did not want to go home.","zh":"去年夏天我们去了趟海边，路途很长。飞机很快就到，可从机场进城却花了几个小时。我妹妹得跑去赶末班车，还差点让我在湿台阶上滑一跤。我们打算第二天早上逛一座老城。那是我记得最清楚的一段：窄窄的街、矮矮的门，还有从海上吹来的暖风。那一周好像没什么能让人扫兴。就算下起雨来，我们也只是走慢一点，还笑个不停。我们都不想回家。"},"turn":{"tw":[["act",0],["better",3],["change",2],["hard",6],["bit",0],["bottom",3],["move",2],["enough",6],["grow",0]],"en":"The road made a sharp turn at the bottom of the hill, and we had to slow down. My father took each bend slowly, because the surface was hard and worn. A bit of rain had made it worse. Nothing could stop the car from sliding a little. He said the car would act strangely if we went too fast, and we did not have enough time to change a wheel. So he let me move over and take a turn at the wheel on the straight part. I grew more careful that day. We were both better drivers by the time we reached home.","zh":"山路在山脚下拐了个急弯，我们只好减速。每个弯我爸都开得很慢，因为路面又硬又旧。一点雨让它更糟。没什么能挡住车子稍微打滑。他说开太快车就会不听使唤，而我们又没时间换轮胎。于是他让我挪过去，在直路上由我开一段。那天我变得谨慎多了。到家的时候，我们俩都开得比以前好了。"},"view":{"tw":[["catch",0],["expect",3],["look",2],["beyond",6],["consider",3],["guess",3],["think",2],["clear",6],["position",0]],"en":"We climbed the hill to catch the view before it got dark. From that position the whole valley lay below us, clear to the far edge. You could look beyond the woods and guess where the river turned. I had not expected so much green. I began to consider how many people must have stood here before. My brother said he could not think of a better place. A cool wind came up, and the air felt thin and fresh. We stayed until the light went, and even then we did not want to leave. It was the kind of evening you remember for years.","zh":"我们爬上山，赶在天黑前看那片风景。站在那个位置，整个山谷都在脚下，一直到天边都清清楚楚。你可以望过树林，猜猜河在哪儿拐弯。我没料到会有这么多绿色。我开始想，从前有多少人站过这里。我弟弟说他想不出比这更好的地方。起了凉风，空气又薄又清。我们待到天光散尽，那时也不想走。这样的傍晚，能让人记上好多年。"},"visit":{"tw":[["call",3],["order",3],["meet",2],["trip",6],["see",3],["frequent",3],["stay",2],["attend",6],["chat",0]],"en":"On Sunday we paid a short visit to our neighbour. My mother made the call first to see if she was well enough for guests. We had to order some cakes on the way and pick them up at the shop. It was a small trip, but we liked to go. Our neighbour would meet us at the door and chat about her garden for an hour. She was a frequent host and never let us stay quiet. We would attend to whatever she asked and see to the tea. I always left feeling lighter than when I came.","zh":"星期天我们去看望了邻居，短坐一会儿。我妈先打了个电话，看她身体好点没有，能不能待客。路上我们还得订几块蛋糕，再到店里取。这一趟不远，但我们乐意去。邻居会在门口迎我们，然后聊上她园子里的花花草草，一聊就是一个钟头。她常常请客，从不让我们冷场。她让做什么我们就帮着做什么，再张罗茶水。每次走的时候，我都比来时轻松。"},"wash":{"tw":[["race",0],["pan",3],["clean",2],["brush",6],["lap",0],["soak",3],["cover",2],["drain",6],["laundry",0]],"en":"After dinner I had to wash the dishes while my sister dealt with the laundry. The pan had burned a little, so I had to soak it first. Then I took a brush to the hard marks and worked until the metal was clean. Water ran over the edge and began to cover the floor near the drain. The cat came to lap the water from the floor. My little brother ran a race around the table and splashed my legs. He thought it was funny. I let him have his fun, then went back to the sink and finished the rest.","zh":"晚饭后我得洗碗，我妹妹去弄要洗的衣服。锅底糊了一点，我先把它泡上。然后我拿刷子对着那些硬印子刷，直到锅底干净。水从边上漫出来，开始淹到下水道附近的地板。猫过来舔地上的水。我弟弟绕着桌子跑了一圈，把我的腿溅湿了。他觉得好玩。我让他闹了一阵，又回到水池边把剩下的洗完。"},"watch":{"tw":[["catch",0],["test",3],["shift",2],["why",6],["check",2],["wake",3],["surveillance",2],["look",6],["follow",0]],"en":"My uncle worked the night watch at a warehouse, and his shift began at ten. Every hour he had to check the doors and look at the small screen by the gate. The cameras gave him a kind of surveillance he did not enjoy. The alarm system gave a short test every evening. Once he had to follow a man along the fence and catch him at the corner. That night he could not wake me, but he told me the story the next day. I asked him why he stayed. He said a quiet job was a good job, and he would keep the watch as long as he could.","zh":"我叔在一间仓库上夜班，十点交接。每个钟头他都要查门，看一眼门口那台小屏幕。那些摄像头让他有种被盯着看的感觉，他并不喜欢。警报系统每晚都会做一次短测试。有一回，他得沿着围栏跟住一个人，在拐角处把他抓住。那天晚上他没能叫醒我，第二天才把这事讲给我听。我问他为什么还干这个。他说清静的活儿就是好活儿，能守多久他就守多久。"},"wear":{"tw":[["bear",0],["black",3],["act",2],["jacket",6],["break",0],["blue",3],["dress",2],["attire",6],["tire",0]],"en":"On a cold morning I could not decide what to wear. My old jacket had begun to break at the shoulder, and the blue dress I liked was much too thin. I did not want to act as if it did not matter. My mother said the black coat would bear the wind better, and that was the right attire for the day. She helped me into the jacket and checked the collar. I did not want to tire her with so many questions. In the end I wore the warm one and left. Outside it was still dark, and the frost lay on the gate.","zh":"一个冷早上，我拿不定主意穿什么。我那件旧外套肩膀开始开线，我喜欢的那条蓝裙子又太薄。我不想装得好像这无所谓。我妈说黑大衣更挡风，那天穿这个正合适。她帮我套上外套，看了看领子。我本不想拿一堆问题烦她，可她很耐心。最后我穿了那件暖和的出了门。外面天还黑着，门口的草上结着霜。"},"wet":{"tw":[["tight",0],["water",3],["change",2],["dry",1],["rain",6],["stiff",0],["sprinkle",3],["cool",6],["moisture",0]],"en":"The rain came in the afternoon and left the yard wet for hours. My shoes were tight and heavy with water, so I had to change them at the door. I hung my coat by the fire to dry, but the cloth stayed stiff and cold. A light sprinkle fell again just before evening. The cool air brought a little moisture into the room, and the windows felt damp. I stayed inside and listened to it on the roof. My mother said the weather would not last, and she was right. By morning the stones were dry again.","zh":"下午下起了雨，把院子打湿了好几个钟头。我的鞋又紧又重，全是水，进门就得换掉。我把外套挂在火边想烘干，布却一直又硬又凉。傍晚前，又飘了一阵小雨。凉气把一点湿意带进屋里，窗子摸上去潮潮的。我待在屋里，听着屋顶上的雨声。我妈说这天气长不了，她说对了。到早上，石头又干了。"},"wheel":{"tw":[["roll",0],["bowl",3],["force",2],["rear",6],["cycle",0],["ordinary",3],["machine",2],["brake",6],["rack",0]],"en":"The rear wheel of my bicycle began to rub against the brake, so I took the whole thing to the shop. An ordinary machine like mine still needs care, the man said. He put the frame in a rack and let the wheel roll on its own. I had to use some force to turn it, which showed where it was bent. He worked like a small cycle of small steps: lift, turn, and check. At last it spun freely. The shop smelled of oil and dust. He would not take money, so I left him a bowl of fruit from our garden.","zh":"我自行车后轮开始蹭刹车，我就整车推去了店里。那人说，像我这种普通机器也得照顾。他把车架架在架子上，让轮子自己转。我得使点劲才转得动，这一转就知道哪儿弯了。他干活像个小小的循环，一步一步来：抬起来、转一转、再查一查。最后轮子转得很顺。店里满是机油和灰尘的味道。他不肯收钱，我就把院子里摘的一碗水果留给了他。"},"whole":{"tw":[["altogether",0],["complex",3],["object",2],["half",1],["rest",6],["solid",0],["compound",3],["unit",3]],"en":"The old farm was a whole world of its own, made of several buildings joined into one compound. A solid stone wall ran all the way around it. My father treated the farm as a single unit, and he knew every part of it. Half of the roof needed work, and the rest would last a few more years. In spring the water came up from below. He said fixing it altogether was a complex job, not something one man could do in a week. The main object of his plan was simple: keep the yard dry. He would not rest until it was done.","zh":"那座旧农场自成一个小世界，几栋房子连成一片院子。一道结实的石墙绕了一圈。我爸把它当成一个整体，每一处他都熟。屋顶有一半要修，剩下的还能再撑几年。春天水会从底下冒上来。他说要整修下来是件复杂的事，不是一个人一周能干完的。他计划的主要目标很简单：让院子保持干燥。活儿不完，他就不肯歇。"},"win":{"tw":[["advance",0],["carry",3],["victory",2],["lose",1],["clinch",6],["gain",0],["hit",3],["chance",6],["acquire",0]],"en":"Our small team did not expect to win against the older players. We had to advance slowly and wait for a chance to hit the ball past them. In the second half my brother began to carry the whole side. One good shot helped us clinch the game at the last minute. The victory was small but real. Even the manager, who hated to lose, smiled at the end. We did not gain much money from it, but we did acquire something better: the belief that we could do it again. We shook hands with the other side and walked home in the dark.","zh":"我们这支小队伍没指望能赢那些年纪更大的对手。我们只能慢慢推进，等机会把球打到他们身后。下半场我弟弟开始一个人扛起全队。最后关头一个好球帮我们把比赛拿下。这场胜利不大，却是真的。连那个最输不起的教练，最后也笑了。我们没挣到多少钱，却得到了更好的东西：相信自己还能再来一次。我们跟对手握了手，摸黑走回家。"},"wish":{"tw":[["care",0],["hope",3],["express",2],["ask",6],["like",0],["please",3],["order",2],["tell",6],["want",0]],"en":"At the end of the meal my sister made a wish and blew out the candles. She would not tell us what it was, though we all asked. My mother said she hoped it would come true. To please her, I had ordered a small cake in the morning, the kind she likes best. Nobody wanted to leave the table. I tried to express how much that quiet evening meant to me, but the words did not come. So I only said I cared about her, and that was enough. The room felt warm even after the candles were out.","zh":"饭快吃完时，我妹妹许了个愿，吹灭了蜡烛。她不肯告诉我们许的什么愿，尽管我们都问了。我妈说但愿能成真。为了让她高兴，我早上订了个小蛋糕，是她最喜欢的那种。谁都不想离桌。我想说这个安静的晚上对我有多重要，可话到嘴边说不出来。于是我只好说我惦记她，这就够了。即便蜡烛灭了，屋里还是暖的。"},"work":{"tw":[["act",0],["answer",3],["fix",2],["idle",1],["well",6],["bring",0],["break",3],["own",6],["form",0]],"en":"For my first week at work I did not have much to do. The owner of the shop told me to act as if I had been there for years. My job was to fix small things: a broken lamp, a door that would not close, a table that stood badly. If I was idle too long, he would call me over and give me a new form to fill in. He would not answer questions during busy hours. The shop was small and warm. By Friday he said I had done well, and that he might bring me on full time.","zh":"上班的第一周，我没多少事做。店老板让我装得像是已经在这儿干了很多年。我的活儿是修些小东西：一盏坏灯、一扇关不严的门、一张放不平的桌子。我要是闲太久，他就把我叫过去，给我一张新表格填。忙的时候他是不回答问题的。店里又小又暖。到了周五，他说我干得不错，还说也许让我转正。"},"worry":{"tw":[["care",0],["fear",3],["mind",2],["say",6],["concern",0],["burden",3],["rub",2],["blame",6],["interest",0]],"en":"My mother began to worry when my brother did not come home by dark. She tried to hide her fear, but she kept looking at the door. In her mind she was already out in the street, searching for him. Her only concern was that something had gone wrong. I told her I would care for him, whatever had happened, and not to take the whole burden on herself. She would rub her hands together and say nothing. At last the phone rang, and we learned he had only missed the last bus. My father began to blame himself for letting him go alone. That night she had no interest in her dinner.","zh":"天黑了弟弟还没回家，我妈开始担心。她想藏住怕，可眼睛老往门口瞟。在她心里，人已经跑到街上找他去了。她只担心是不是出了什么事。我跟她说，不管发生了什么，我会照顾他，别把这份担子都压在自己身上。她只是搓着手，一句话不说。最后电话响了，我们才知道他只是错过了末班车。我爸开始怪自己不该让他一个人去。那之后她对晚饭一点兴趣都没有。"},"write":{"tw":[["save",0],["arrange",3],["record",2],["read",6],["pen",0],["cross",3],["trace",2],["book",6],["spell",0]],"en":"Every Sunday my grandmother would write a long letter to her sister. She kept a special pen for it and always used the same blue paper. I would read the words over her shoulder and watch her cross out a line, then write it again. She liked to arrange her thoughts first, so she would trace the shape of each word in the air before it went down. Each letter held a small record of the week. She told me to save every letter I ever received. Now I have a whole book of hers, and I still cannot spell some of the names she wrote.","zh":"每个星期天，我奶奶都会给她妹妹写一封长信。她为写信留着一支专门的笔，纸也总用同一种蓝的。我会从她肩后读那些字，看她划掉一行，再重写。她喜欢先理清想法，所以落笔前会在空气里描一描每个字的形状。每一封信都像一小份关于那一周的记录。她叫我把我收到的每一封信都留着。如今我有她整整一本书的信，可有些她写过的名字，我还是拼不出来。"},"student":{"tw":[["study",4],["pupil",0],["theologian",3],["intellectual",2],["graduate",6],["scholar",3],["school",6]],"en":"As a student I was never the best in the school, but I liked to study. One of my teachers was a quiet scholar who had once wanted to be a theologian. She treated every pupil the same and never raised her voice. She was an intellectual in the truest sense: she read for hours and asked good questions. When my brother had to graduate, she came to the small party at our house. Years later she told me that teaching was the only work she had ever wanted. She had a way of making a hard idea feel simple. I still think of her.","zh":"做学生的时候，我从来不是学校里最好的，但我喜欢念书。我有一位老师，是个安静的学者，年轻时还想当神学家。她对每个学生都一样，从不提高嗓门。她是个真正的知识分子：一读就是几个钟头，问题也问得好。我弟弟毕业时，她来参加了我们家那个小聚会。多年以后她告诉我，教书是她唯一想干的事。她有种本事，能把难懂的道理讲得简单。我到今天还会想起她。"},"tooth":{"tw":[["dental",4],["canine",3],["bone",2],["scar",6],["fang",3],["structure",2],["claw",6]],"en":"The dentist looked at my back tooth and said it would need a small filling. She showed me the structure of a jaw on a poster behind her head. She said the bone under the gum was still strong. A dog has a long canine and sharp fangs, she said, while a person has flat teeth for grinding. I had a small scar on my chin from a fall as a child, and she asked about it. I told her the story of the dog whose claw had caught me, and she laughed. Then she began the dental work, and I closed my eyes.","zh":"牙医看了看我后面的牙，说得补一小块。她指着身后墙上的图，给我讲牙床的结构。她说，牙龈底下的骨头还结实。她说，狗有长长的犬齿和尖尖的獠牙，而人的牙是平的，用来磨东西。我下巴上有道小疤，是小时候摔的，她问起这事。我给她讲了那条狗用爪子勾住我的经过，她笑了。然后她开始做牙，我闭上了眼睛。"},"voice":{"tw":[["vocal",4],["sound",2],["bass",3],["express",2],["tone",6],["pronounce",2],["touch",6]],"en":"In the school choir my sister had the strongest voice. She could hold a low note in a deep bass tone that made the whole room quiet. The teacher said she should train her vocal cords, but never force them. She learned to pronounce the old words clearly, and to express each line with feeling. Sometimes she would touch my arm and sing a note for me alone. The sound of it stayed in my head all day. She never sang for praise, only for the joy of it. I could not sing at all, but I loved to listen. It was enough for me.","zh":"在学校合唱队里，我妹妹的嗓音最亮。她能用一个低沉的男低音拖住一个音符，让整间屋子都静下来。老师说她的声带要练，但不能硬撑。她学会了把那些老词咬清楚，还学会每一句都唱出感情。有时她会碰碰我的胳膊，单独为我唱一个音。那声音在我脑子里响一整天。她唱歌不是为了夸奖，只是为了那份高兴。我一点也不会唱，可我特别爱听。对我来说，这就够了。"},"war":{"tw":[["warrior",4],["warfare",0],["campaign",2],["peace",1],["military",6],["conflict",2],["army",6]],"en":"In history class we studied a long war and the men who fought in it. The teacher said every warrior on both sides believed he was right. The campaign had lasted years, and the whole army had marched through snow. We read about the new kinds of warfare that appeared in that time. The museum held a military uniform with a hole in the chest. Afterwards I walked home slowly and thought about peace. It was only a lesson, but it stayed with me. That night I could not sleep, because the old conflict felt close to me, as if it had happened yesterday.","zh":"历史课上，我们学了一场漫长的战争和在战争中打仗的人。老师说，两边每个战士都相信自己是正义的。这场战役打了好些年，整支军队踏过雪地行军。我们读到那时出现的各种新式战法。博物馆里陈列着一件军装，胸口有个洞。下课后我慢慢走回家，想着和平。这不过是一堂课，却留在了我心里。那晚我睡不着，因为那段旧日冲突离我很近，仿佛是昨天才发生的。"},"single":{"tw":[["ace",0],["hit",2],["double",1],["individual",0],["digit",2],["same",6],["exclusive",0]],"en":"He served an ace on the first point, and the crowd stood up. It was not a single good shot but a whole run of them. He would hit the ball so hard that his opponent could only watch. The score went up to double figures before the first set was over. Every individual in the stand was on his feet. He was the exclusive owner of that court for one afternoon. At the end he raised one digit to the sky, the same gesture his father had used. I have never seen a player so calm.","zh":"第一个球他就发了个直接得分，看台上的人全站了起来。那不是一个好球，而是一连串好球。他抽得那么狠，对手只能干看着。第一盘还没打完，比分就上了两位数。看台上每一个人都站了起来。那天下午，这片球场好像只属于他一个人。结束时他朝天竖起一根手指，跟他父亲当年一模一样。我从没见过这么沉着的球员。"},"spend":{"tw":[["drop",0],["blow",3],["pay",2],["raise",6],["pass",0],["save",3],["alone",6],["expend",0]],"en":"He would spend his whole wage in three days and then live on bread for the rest of the month. He liked to pay for his friends and would never let them drop a coin in the pot. A single blow of bad luck could leave him with nothing. He would raise a glass and pass it round the table, laughing. He could not save, and he did not want to. Alone at the end of the night, he would count what was left and expend the last of it on a room.","zh":"他三天就能把一个月的工钱花光，剩下的日子啃面包。他喜欢替朋友付账，从不让他们往钱罐里丢一个子儿。一次倒霉就能让他两手空空。他会举起杯子，笑着在桌上传一圈。他攒不下钱，也不想攒。夜深人散，他一个人数数还剩多少，把最后一点花在一间房上。"},"stage":{"tw":[["leg",0],["plane",3],["state",2],["tour",6],["present",0],["wing",3],["travel",2],["first",6]],"en":"The band would travel from town to town, and every stage was different. On the first night the singer's leg was still bad, so he sat on a chair. A plane flew low over the hall and shook the lights. The tour had begun in a poor state, and nobody was sure it would last. A young woman stood in the wing and watched, waiting to be called. They would present the same songs every night, and still people came. By the last show they had played to a full house in every town.","zh":"这支乐队一个镇一个镇地跑，每一处台子都不一样。头一晚主唱的腿还没好利索，只好坐在椅子上唱。一架飞机低低掠过礼堂上方，震得灯都在晃。巡演一开始就不太顺，谁也不敢说撑不撑得住。一个年轻女人站在侧幕后面看着，等着被叫上场。他们每晚都唱同样的歌，来的人还是不少。到最后一场，他们每到一个镇都是满座。"},"station":{"tw":[["post",0],["locate",3],["move",2],["radio",6],["send",0],["fort",3],["position",2],["bus",6]],"en":"The small station stood on the cliff, where a fort had once been. A radio sent the weather news to the boats below every morning. It was hard to locate from the sea, and the men would move along the path with a lamp. My father had a post there for six years. He would send his report and then watch the bus come up the hill. From his position at the window he could see the whole bay. I still walk up that path sometimes. It was a fine place to work.","zh":"那座小站建在崖上，从前那儿有座炮台。每天早晨，一台无线电把天气消息发给下面的渔船。从海上很难找到它，人们得提着灯沿小路走。我爸在那儿守了六年。他会发完报告，再看着公交车爬上山坡。从窗边他的位置上，能望见整个海湾。有时我还会走上那条小路。那是个干活的好地方。"},"store":{"tw":[["shop",0],["bottle",3],["hardware",2],["warehouse",6],["fund",0],["issue",3],["retail",6],["memory",0]],"en":"The old store sold everything from a bottle of oil to a bag of nails, and people came from the next town for it. Half the shop was a warehouse of boxes, and the other half was pure hardware, crowded on the walls. The owner would issue a bill by hand and put the money in a tin for the fund. In those days retail was a slow and personal trade. He knew every customer by name. Now the store lives only in my memory. When he died, his son tried to keep the place open.","zh":"这家老店什么都卖，从一瓶油到一袋钉子，人们从邻镇赶来。铺子一半是堆箱子的仓库，另一半全是五金，挂满了墙。老板会手写一张单据，把钱放进铁盒里当公积金。那时候做零售是件慢悠悠、讲人情的事。他叫得出每位客人的名字。如今这家店只活在我的记忆里了。他去世后，他儿子还想把店撑下去。"},"story":{"tw":[["history",0],["legend",3],["record",2],["novel",6],["report",0],["myth",3],["picture",6],["tale",0]],"en":"My grandmother would tell us a story every night, and the same tale would change each time. She knew the history of the whole village and had a legend for every stone. There was one about a hidden box that everyone said was a myth, though she swore it was true. She would read a novel in the afternoon and turn it into a picture for us at night. I began to write her stories down. The record I kept is the only report of those evenings. I still open that book when I want her voice in the room.","zh":"奶奶每天晚上都给我们讲一个故事，同一个故事每回讲得都不一样。她知道整个村子的来历，每块石头都有一段传说。有一个讲的是个藏起来的箱子，人人都说那是瞎编的，她却一口咬定是真的。她下午读小说，晚上就把它讲成我们眼前的一幅画。我开始把她的故事记下来。我留下的那份记录，是那些夜晚唯一的记载。想她的时候，我就翻开那本书。"},"sweet":{"tw":[["fresh",0],["candy",3],["course",2],["dry",1],["honey",6],["confection",0],["taste",2],["ginger",6]],"en":"The cake was too sweet for me, but my brother ate two pieces. My mother would use honey instead of sugar, and a little ginger to give it a taste. She would serve it as the last course of the meal. The shop down the road sold a small candy for a penny, and we would buy one each. Her sweets were never dry and always fresh. A neighbour once said she could turn any fruit into a confection. I learned to bake from her, and I still use her recipe.","zh":"这蛋糕对我来说太甜了，可我弟弟吃了两块。我妈会用蜂蜜代替糖，再放一点姜提味。她会把它留作饭后最后一道。街那头的铺子一分钱卖一颗小糖，我们一人买一颗。她做的甜点从不发干，总是新鲜的。有个邻居说过，她能把任何果子做成糖点。我跟着她学会了烘焙，她的方子我到现在还在用。"},"tax":{"tw":[["assess",0],["tariff",3],["charge",2],["pension",6],["task",0],["excise",3],["strain",2],["pay",6]],"en":"Each spring the man from the office would come to assess the shop, and my father would spend a week getting the papers ready. There was a tax on everything: a tariff on the imported tea, an excise on the drink, a small charge on each sale. The work was a heavy strain on him, and it was never a task he enjoyed. Half his pension, he said, went back to the state in one form or another. Yet he would pay it without a word. He said a country costs money, like everything else.","zh":"每年春天，事务所的人都会来给店铺估税，我爸要花一个星期把材料备齐。什么都要交税：进口茶叶有关税，酒有消费税，每一笔买卖还有一笔小费。这活儿压得他很累，也从来不是他乐意干的事。他说，他那份养老金有一半以各种名目又交了回去。可他还是一声不响地交了。他说，国家也是要花钱的，跟别的都一样。"},"teach":{"tw":[["instruct",0],["ground",3],["inform",2],["educate",6],["thatch",0],["coach",3],["pirate",2],["understand",6]],"en":"The old thatcher would teach his trade to anyone who would listen, and he had one young man to instruct that year. He would ground him in the basics first: how to cut the straw, how to lay it, how to tie it down. He wanted the boy to understand the reason behind each move, not just to copy it. He would inform the customer of every step. He was not there to educate anyone, he said, only to fix the house. A coach of the village team once asked him why the roof was so thick, and he said it was to keep out the rain. Some people thought him a pirate with his prices, but he was honest to the last pound.","zh":"那位老茅匠愿意把手艺教给任何肯听的人，那年他带了一个年轻人。他先让他打基础：怎么割草，怎么铺，怎么捆紧。他要这孩子弄懂每个动作背后的道理，而不只是照做。村里球队的教练有一次问他屋顶为什么那么厚，他说是为了挡雨。每一步他都会跟主家讲清楚。他说他不是来教书的，只是来修房子。有人觉得他要价像海盗，可他老实到最后一镑。"},"total":{"tw":[["add",0],["average",3],["count",2],["million",6],["full",0],["whole",5],["least",6],["entire",0]],"en":"At the end of the fair the whole village would count the money for the church roof. They would add up every box and write the total on a board by the door. The least they had ever raised was twenty pounds, and this year it was a hundred. A million would not have surprised them. The average gift was small, but the hall was full both nights, and the entire town seemed to help. My mother said it was the whole village that paid for that roof. We were all proud of that little board.","zh":"集市结束时，全村人会一起清点为修教堂屋顶募来的钱。他们把每只箱子里的钱加在一起，把总数写在门口的板子上。他们最少的一次募到二十镑，今年是一百。就算是一百万他们也不会吃惊。捐款平均下来不多，可两个晚上礼堂都坐满了，好像全城的人都来帮忙了。我妈说，掏钱修那屋顶的是整个村子。那块小木牌，我们都为它骄傲。"},"travel":{"tw":[["move",0],["fall",3],["motion",2],["service",6],["trip",0],["fly",3],["access",6],["journey",0]],"en":"The only service to the village was a bus that left at dawn. The journey took six hours, and the road would fall and rise along the valley. We would move slowly, with the motion of the old engine rocking us to sleep. A bird would fly beside the window for a mile or more. For many people the bus was their only access to a hospital or a market. My grandmother made that trip four times a year. She would travel with a small bag and a paper of food, and never once complain.","zh":"通往村子的唯一一趟车，是天不亮就出发的公交。这趟行程要六个钟头，路顺着山谷一起一落。车走得很慢，旧发动机的晃动把我们摇睡。有只鸟会跟着车窗飞上一里多地。对很多人来说，这趟车是他们去医院或集市的唯一门路。我奶奶一年要坐四回。她总带着一个小包和一包干粮上路，从不抱怨一句。"},"trouble":{"tw":[["bother",0],["hell",3],["hurt",2],["without",6],["pain",0],["matter",3],["affect",2],["problem",0]],"en":"We had trouble with the car in the middle of nowhere, and it was a problem we could not solve. There was no light and no water, and the cold began to affect us all. The pain in my father's back was getting worse. He said it was no matter and told us not to bother him. It hurt him to bend, but he would not say a word. To go on without help was the only way. It was a small hell of an hour before a lorry stopped.","zh":"车在前不着村后不着店的地方出了毛病，这是我们解决不了的问题。没有灯，也没有水，寒气开始侵到每个人身上。我爸背上的疼越来越厉害。他说没什么要紧，叫我们别烦他。他一弯腰就疼，却一个字也不说。没有外援，只能硬往前走。熬了像地狱般的一个钟头，才有一辆卡车停下来。"},"walk":{"tw":[["pass",0],["foot",3],["play",2],["ride",1],["sit",6],["step",3],["travel",2],["room",6]],"en":"Every evening my grandfather would take a slow walk to the end of the lane and back. He would pass the old school, where he used to play as a boy, and stop to watch the children. His foot dragged a little now, and he would step carefully over the roots. He would not ride; the walk was the point. If I came with him, we would sit on a low wall and watch the light go. There was room for both of us and our thoughts. He would travel only with his stick and a quiet word.","zh":"每天傍晚，爷爷都会慢慢走到巷子尽头再走回来。他会路过那座旧学校，小时候他就在那儿玩耍，如今会停下来看看孩子们。他的一只脚现在有点拖，遇到树根会小心地迈过去。他不骑车，走路才是正经事。要是我陪他，我们就在一道矮墙上坐下，看天光一点点褪去。那地方容得下我们俩，也容得下我们的心事。他上路只带一根拐杖和一句轻话。"},"want":{"tw":[["need",2],["cry",3],["miss",2],["sure",6],["wish",3],["hope",3],["demand",2],["desire",0]],"en":"She did not want much: a room of her own, and someone to talk to. She would cry at night, when she thought nobody could hear. She would miss the house where she had lived for fifty years. She was sure her family would come, though they never did. She had a wish to see the sea once more, and a deep desire to die at home. She would demand nothing, and that was the hardest part. I used to sit with her and hope for the same things she did. She only needed to be heard.","zh":"她要的不多：一间自己的屋子，一个能说话的人。夜里她以为没人听见，就会哭。她会想念那座住了五十年的房子。她确信家里人一定会来，可他们从没来过。她有个心愿，想再看一次海；还有个很深的愿望，想死在家里。她什么也不强求，而这一点最难。我那时常坐在她身边，跟她盼着同样的事。她要的，只是有人听她说。"},"warm":{"tw":[["quick",0],["chafe",3],["change",2],["cool",1],["cold",6],["strong",0],["dry",6],["tender",0]],"en":"The night was cold, and my grandfather would build a fire to keep the room warm. He had a quick way with the wood and never used too much. He would chafe his hands over the flames and then hold them to his face. The change in the room was slow but sure. A strong wind came down the chimney, and the fire would fall and rise again. He would dry his coat by the hearth and then sit down. His voice was tender when he talked about my grandmother. It was the cool of the evening, he said, that he loved most.","zh":"那天晚上很冷，爷爷会生起火来，让屋里暖和。他劈柴有一套，从不烧多。他会在火苗上搓搓手，再把手贴到脸上。屋里的变化很慢，却实实在在。一股强风从烟囱灌下来，火一低又窜起来。他会把外套在炉边烘干，然后坐下。他讲起我奶奶的时候，声音很柔。他说，黄昏那点凉意，是他最喜欢的。"},"weather":{"tw":[["brave",0],["wave",3],["sail",2],["rain",6],["endure",0],["wind",3],["lean",2],["cold",6]],"en":"Bad weather had kept the boats in the harbour for a week, and the sea was still rough. The wind would lean the old trees almost to the ground. Rain came in across the bay in long grey lines. My grandfather was brave in a quiet way; he had learned to endure the long nights at sea. He would sail out when others stayed home. A great wave once took the nets and nearly took him. He came back cold and silent, and never spoke of it. The village remembered that night for many winters.","zh":"连着一个星期，坏天气把船都困在港里，海面还是很凶。风把老树吹得几乎贴到地面。雨从海湾那边成片成片地斜过来，灰蒙蒙的。爷爷有一种不声张的胆气；他早学会了挨过海上漫长的夜。别人留在家里，他偏要出海。有一次一个巨浪卷走了渔网，差点也把他卷走。他回来时又冷又沉默，一字不提。那一夜，村里人记了好多个冬天。"},"white":{"tw":[["clean",0],["bone",3],["man",2],["black",1],["green",6],["blank",0],["chalk",3],["brown",6]],"en":"In the art room the teacher gave every student a sheet of clean white paper. She would draw with chalk, a black line here, a green and a brown shape there. My page stayed blank for a long time. Beside me an old man was making a picture of a bone, and it was very good. He said a white space could say as much as a dark one. The room smelled of chalk and old wood. When the bell rang, I had only drawn a few lines, but I kept the sheet.","zh":"美术教室里，老师给每个学生发了一张干净的白纸。她会用粉笔画，这儿一道黑线，那儿一个绿的和一个棕色的形状。我的纸空白了好半天。旁边一位老人正画一根骨头，画得非常好。他说，一片白就跟一片黑一样能说话。屋里飘着粉笔和旧木头的味道。下课铃响时，我只画了几笔，可那张纸我留了下来。"},"woman":{"tw":[["char",0],["wife",3],["class",2],["man",1],["girl",6],["broad",3],["adult",2],["mother",6]],"en":"The woman who kept the vegetable stall had once been a char, cleaning offices at night. She was the wife of a sailor, and her mother had run the same stall before her. A class of girls from the school came by every Tuesday, and she would give them each an apple. The man at the next stall said she had broad hands and a soft heart. She treated every adult the same, rich or poor. I bought from her for years. When she died, the market was never quite the same place.","zh":"守着那个菜摊的女人，从前是个打扫办公室的杂役，夜里做清洁。她是一个水手的妻子，她的母亲从前也摆这个摊。每个星期二，有一班女学生会路过，她会给她们一人一个苹果。隔壁摊的男人说她手掌宽厚，心也软。她待每个成年人都一个样，不管穷富。我跟她买了好些年。她去世以后，那个集市就再也不是原来的样子了。"},"shut":{"tw":[["close",0],["draw",3],["open",1],["stop",6],["closed",0],["seal",3],["run",6]],"en":"The shop was shut, and a small sign said closed for the day. I tried to open the door, then gave up. The wind had begun to draw the clouds across the sky. I ran to the next street to find another one, but the shutters were down there too. I wanted to close my eyes, to stop and think, but the rain pushed me on. A man was sealing a box by the wall. I asked him when the shops would open again. He did not know either, and he said the whole town closed early in such weather. I walked home with wet shoes and no bread.","zh":"店已经关了，一块小牌子写着今天歇业。我试着推门，后来作罢。风开始把云往天上拉。我跑到下一条街想找另一家，可那里的卷帘门也拉下了。我想停下来想想，雨却推着我往前走。有个人正在墙边封一只箱子。我问他店什么时候再开。他也不知道，只说这种天气里全镇都早早关门。我湿着鞋回了家，什么也没买到。"},"slight":{"tw":[["little",0],["snub",3],["dismiss",2],["sharp",6],["thin",5],["sudden",6],["fragile",0]],"en":"She gave me a slight as she passed, a small snub I did not expect. It was a little thing, and yet it stung. Her face was thin and sharp in the cold light. I wanted to dismiss it, the way one dismisses a sudden noise, but I could not. There was something fragile under her calm. I stood there and said nothing. Later I learned that she had been ill for weeks and had not told anyone. The slight had cost her more than it cost me. I never mentioned it, and neither did she.","zh":"她走过时对我冷淡了一下，那是我没料到的一次小小怠慢。本是件小事，却扎人。冷光里她的脸又瘦又利。我想把它置之不理，就像不去理会一声突响，可我做不到。她的平静底下有什么脆弱的东西。我站在原处，什么也没说。后来我才知道，她病了好几个星期，谁也没告诉。那点冷淡，她付出的代价比我还大。我从没提过，她也没有。"},"small":{"tw":[["little",5],["size",2],["big",1],["well",6],["low",0],["main",6],["minor",0]],"en":"A small boat took us across the river. Its size surprised me; it looked too little for three people. My father said a big boat was not always safer. The main thing was to keep it low in the water and row well. There was one minor leak near the front, which he fixed with a cloth. We reached the other bank before noon. On the far side a dog was waiting, as if it had known we were coming. It followed us all the way to the village. I was twelve that summer, and I still think of that river as mine.","zh":"一条小船把我们载过河。它的尺寸让我吃惊，看着太小，装不下三个人。我父亲说大船不一定就更安全。要紧的是让它压得低低的，把桨划好。船头有个小漏洞，他用一块布补上了。中午前我们就到了对岸。那边有条狗在等着，好像早知道我们要来。它一路跟到村里。那年夏天我十二岁，到现在我还觉得那条河是我的。"},"smile":{"tw":[["grin",3],["beam",3],["express",2],["laugh",6],["sneer",3],["grimace",2],["touch",6]],"en":"She gave me a small smile at the door. It was not a grin and not a laugh, only the quiet way she had of showing that she was glad. Her face would beam for a moment, then go still. She never used a sneer, and I never saw her grimace. To express warmth, she would touch your arm and say nothing. I miss that more than anything. She is gone now, and the house is quiet in a different way. I still open the door slowly, as if she might be standing there.","zh":"在门口她对我微微一笑。那不是咧嘴的笑，也不是大笑，只是她那种安静地表示高兴的方式。她的脸会亮一下，随即又静下来。她从不用冷笑，我也没见过她皱脸。她要表示亲切时，就碰一下你的胳膊，什么也不说。我最想念的就是这个。她如今不在了，屋子里静得不一样。我开门时还是会慢一点，好像她可能就站在那儿。"},"snow":{"tw":[["blow",0],["flurry",3],["layer",2],["rain",6],["coke",0],["precipitate",2],["fog",6]],"en":"Snow began to fall in the afternoon, at first a light flurry, then a steady rain of white. The wind would blow it against the windows and pile a thick layer on the step. Fog covered the yard before dark. My uncle went out to bring in the coke, and his boots left deep marks in the snow. The cold seemed to precipitate a silence over the whole street. Nobody came to the door that evening. Even the dogs were quiet, and the only sound was the soft weight of the snow itself.","zh":"下午开始下雪，先是一阵轻飘的雪絮，随后成了绵密的白雨。风把它吹到窗上，在台阶上积起厚厚一层。天黑前雾罩住了院子。我叔出去把焦炭搬进来，靴子在雪里留下深深的印子。寒气仿佛让整条街一下子沉入寂静。那天傍晚没人来敲门。连狗都静了，唯一的声响就是雪本身落下的那点分量。"},"sport":{"tw":[["fun",0],["freak",3],["athlete",2],["club",6],["play",2],["pun",3],["feature",0]],"en":"Sport was the one thing he loved. He was no athlete, only a quiet boy who liked to play in the field behind the school. Every club wanted him because he made the games fun. Once he made a pun about the ball, and the whole team laughed. The others called him a freak for joking so much, but never unkindly. The main feature of those afternoons was his laugh. I did not play well, and it never mattered to him. He would wait at the gate until I was ready to walk home.","zh":"运动是他唯一喜欢的事。他算不上运动员，只是个爱在学校后面空地上玩的安静男孩。每个俱乐部都想要他，因为有他在，比赛就有趣。有一次他拿球开了个玩笑，全队都笑了。别人笑他太爱说笑，管他叫怪人，可从没有恶意。那些下午最大的特色就是他的笑声。我玩得不好，他一点也不在意。他会在门口一直等到我准备回家。"},"straight":{"tw":[["flat",0],["stretch",3],["section",2],["round",6],["neat",0],["consecutive",6],["square",0]],"en":"The road ran straight across the flat land for a long stretch. In one section there were neat rows of trees on both sides, all the same height. The fields were square, and the sky above them was round and wide. We drove without stopping for three consecutive hours. It was the straightest road I have ever known. My mother slept in the back, and my father kept his eyes on the white line. I watched the fields and said nothing for hours. When we finally turned off, the whole world seemed to bend.","zh":"那条路笔直地穿过平地，延伸了好长一段。其中有一段，两边是整整齐齐的树，高矮全都一样。田是方方正正的，田上的天又圆又阔。我们一连开了三个钟头没停。那是我见过的最直的一条路。我妈在后座睡着，我爸盯着那条白线。我看了好几个钟头的田野，一句话没说。等我们终于拐下大路，整个世界仿佛都弯了。"},"suggest":{"tw":[["advise",0],["advance",3],["express",2],["indicate",0],["recommend",3],["inform",2],["propose",0]],"en":"My manager would suggest a change and then wait for us to think about it. She liked to advise rather than order, and she would recommend a plan only after we had spoken. Once she asked me to express my own view first. The figures seemed to indicate a slow advance in sales. She would inform the director and propose a small test. I learned a lot from the way she worked. Years later, in another office, I found myself doing the same thing. I would ask a question and then say nothing at all.","zh":"我上司会提一个改动，然后等我们自己去想。她喜欢提建议而不是下命令，只有在我们都发过言之后，她才会推荐一个方案。有一回她让我先说说自己的想法。那些数字似乎显示销量在缓慢上升。她会通知主管，再提个小试验。我从她做事的方式里学了不少。多年后，在另一间办公室，我发现自己也这么做了。我会先问一个问题，然后就什么也不说。"},"surprise":{"tw":[["storm",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["despite",6],["amaze",3],["change",2],["doubt",6]],"en":"The storm came as a surprise to everyone in the village. Despite the warning on the radio, nobody had expected it so early. The change in the sky would amaze even the oldest farmer. I had no doubt that we would lose the roof. My father made a quick act of tying the door and catching the loose shutters. By morning the wind was gone and the street was quiet. We walked outside and found a tree across the road. Nobody was hurt, and that was the only thing that mattered.","zh":"那场风暴让村里每个人都吃了一惊。尽管收音机里报了警，谁也没料到它来得这么早。天上的变化连最老的农夫看了都要吃惊。我毫不怀疑我们会丢掉屋顶。我父亲赶紧动手，把门拴好，抓住松了的窗板。到早上，风停了，街上安静下来。我们走到外面，发现一棵树横在路上。没人受伤，这才是唯一要紧的事。"},"swim":{"tw":[["float",0],["school",3],["travel",2],["surf",6],["drown",0],["crawl",3],["skate",6]],"en":"In summer I would swim in the lake every morning. A school of small fish would float near the shore, and I could see them from above. My brother liked to travel to the coast to surf, but I never learned. He said I swam like a slow crawl and would drown in real waves. In winter we would skate on the same water, hard as glass. Those were the years when the lake was still clean enough to drink. Now there is a fence around it, and a sign with rules.","zh":"夏天我每天早上都到湖里游泳。一群小鱼会浮在岸边，我从上面就能看见。我哥喜欢跑到海边去冲浪，我却一直没学会。他说我游得像慢吞吞的自由泳，到了真正的大浪里非淹死不可。冬天我们就在同一片水上滑冰，硬得像玻璃。那些年湖水还干净得能喝。如今湖周围围了栏，还立了块写满规矩的牌子。"},"tape":{"tw":[["record",2],["cut",3],["attach",2],["video",6],["write",3],["strip",2],["cassette",6]],"en":"I found an old tape in a drawer, a cassette from years ago. On the label was my mother's writing, small and careful. I had to cut a strip of it where it was torn, then attach the ends again. It held a record of a family dinner, and someone had made a short video of the same evening. I played it once and sat still in the dark. I could hear my father laughing at something nobody remembered. I have not played it since, and I never will. Some things are better kept than used.","zh":"我在抽屉里找到一盘旧磁带，是好多年前的那种盒式带。标签是我妈的字。有一处撕了，我得剪下一小条，再把两头接上。里面录着一顿家宴，那个晚上还有人拍了一小段视频。我放了一遍，就一动不动地坐在黑里。我听见我父亲在为什么事笑，而那事谁也不记得了。从那以后我再没放过，也永远不会放了。有些东西留着比用掉更好。"},"thick":{"tw":[["deep",5],["inside",2],["thin",1],["brush",6],["dense",0],["beneath",6],["compact",0]],"en":"The fog was thick over the valley, deep and dense in the low places. Beneath it the fields were hidden, and only the tops of the trees showed. I walked with a thin stick, tapping the path ahead. The brush on both sides grew close and compact, and once I lost the way. Inside the fog everything sounded near. A dog barked somewhere to my left, and then again, closer. I stopped and waited until I could tell which way it came from. The sound led me back to the road, and I never forgot it.","zh":"山谷上罩着浓雾，低处又深又密。雾底下田野都看不见了，只有树梢露出来。我拿着一根细棍，敲着前面的路走。两边的灌木长得又近又密，有一回我迷了路。雾里面，什么声音听着都很近。我左边什么地方有条狗叫了一声，接着又叫，更近了。我停下来，等到能分辨出声音是从哪个方向来的。那声音把我引回了路上，我一直没忘。"},"understand":{"tw":[["read",3],["catch",3],["how",6],["realise",0],["follow",3],["know",6],["see",0]],"en":"I could not understand the letter at first. I read it twice, then a third time, trying to catch the meaning behind the words. I did not know how to answer it. My sister read it too, and she began to realise what had happened. I could follow the facts, but not the feeling. Only later, in the quiet of the evening, did I see what he had tried to say. By then it was too late to write back. I keep the letter in a book, and sometimes I take it out.","zh":"起初我看不懂那封信。我读了两遍，又读第三遍，想抓住字面背后的意思。我不知道该怎么回。我姐也读了，她开始明白发生了什么事。我能跟得上那些事实，却跟不上那份心情。直到后来，在傍晚的安静里，我才看清他想说的是什么。那时再回信已经太晚了。我把信夹在一本书里，有时会拿出来看看。"},"way":{"tw":[["room",0],["fit",3],["choice",2],["direction",0],["form",3],["course",2],["fashion",0]],"en":"There was only one way to fit everything into the small room, and I found it at last. I had no choice but to move the desk and turn it the other way. The direction of the light helped. In this form the space looked twice as big. My mother said it was the fashion now to keep things plain. I took the course she suggested and left the walls bare. For a week the room felt like someone else's. Then one morning it felt like mine, and I stopped moving the furniture.","zh":"要把所有东西塞进这间小屋，只有一种办法，我终于找到了。我别无选择，只能挪开桌子，把它转到另一个方向。光的方向帮了忙。这样一摆，空间看着大了一倍。我妈说如今时兴把东西收拾得素净。我照她提的路子做了，让墙空着。有一个星期，这屋子像别人家的。后来有天早上，它像我的了，我就不再挪家具了。"},"web":{"tw":[["net",0],["tent",3],["object",2],["internet",6],["network",0],["trap",2],["video",6]],"en":"A spider had built a web between the fence and the old tent in the garden. The net was fine as thread, and a small object, a dead fly, hung in the middle. I watched a video about spiders on the internet that evening, and I learned how they make the network strong. It is a kind of trap that never needs repair. In the morning the web was gone. I looked for it again the next day, and the day after that. Nothing stayed in that garden for long.","zh":"一只蜘蛛在篱笆和园里那顶旧帐篷之间结了张网。网丝细得像线，中间挂着个小东西，一只死苍蝇。那天晚上我在网上看了一段讲蜘蛛的视频，知道了它们怎么把这张网织得结实。那是一种从不需要修补的陷阱。到了早上，网不见了。第二天我又去找，第三天也去找。那园子里什么都留不长久。"},"wrong":{"tw":[["damage",0],["treat",2],["right",1],["why",6],["else",6],["amiss",0],["awry",0]],"en":"Something was wrong with the old machine, and I could not say why. Every part looked right, yet the whole thing had gone awry. I checked the damage twice. There was nothing else I could do that night. My father said not to treat it as a great problem, that a small thing was amiss somewhere. In the morning he found it and laughed. A wire had come loose, and it had taken him a single minute. He said most wrong things are smaller than they look. I have remembered that ever since, more than once.","zh":"那台旧机器出了毛病，我说不清是为什么。每个零件看着都对，可整体却失了常。我把损坏的地方查了两遍。那晚我再也做不了别的。我父亲说别把它当成什么大问题，不过是哪儿有点小毛病。第二天早上他找到了，笑起来。原来是一根线松了，他只花了一分钟。他说，大多数出错的事都比看上去要小。这句话我后来记了很久，不止一回想起。"},"zero":{"tw":[["nought",0],["adjust",2],["mean",6],["zip",0],["digit",2],["maximum",6],["null",0]],"en":"The temperature fell to zero before morning, and the little gauge showed a single digit. I had to adjust the setting to its maximum, but it did nothing. The reading stayed at nought. My father said the number did not mean anything at all; it was null, a zip. We put on two coats and went out anyway. The path was hard and bright, and our breath made small clouds. I could not feel my fingers, but I did not want to go back inside. That was the coldest night I can remember, and the house never warmed up the next day.","zh":"天亮前气温降到了零度，小仪表上只显示一个数字。我只好把设定调到最大，可它毫无反应。读数一直停在零。我父亲说这个数根本说明不了什么，是空的，等于没有。我们套上两件外套照样出了门。小路又硬又亮，我们的呼吸结成一小团一小团的白气。我手指都冻麻了，却不想回屋去。那是我记得的最冷的一夜，第二天屋里也一直没暖和起来。"}}});
